t["subzone:shrine-of-the-dormant-flame"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="27,297,27.723.0,49.218.0,39.242.0,19.211.0,41.245.0",["h"]="12e9dc",["n"]="Santuario de la Llama Latente",["s"]="Santuario de la Llama Latente. Encaramado en la cima del pico más alto al noroeste del Valle de los Retos, el Santuario de la Llama Latente es un refugio apartado y venerado por los chamanes de la Horda. Guiados por su solitario guardián, Telf Joolam, los iniciados emprenden la peligrosa ascensión para entrar en comunión con el elemento del fuego y demostrar su maestría espiritual. Llegar al Santuario de la Llama Latente requiere enfrentarse a un sendero estrecho y serpenteante que comienza junto al Río Furia del Sur, en el extremo suroeste de Southfury Watershed. Muy por encima de los riscos rojos de Durotar, la cumbre de la montaña ofrece una vista imponente de las tierras circundantes, aunque un solo paso en falso por el precipicio supone una muerte segura. En este tranquilo refugio deambula Telf Joolam, un ermitaño solitario encargado de supervisar los ritos sagrados. Para los aspirantes a chamán orcos y trols que emprenden el ritual de La llamada del Fuego, el brasero del santuario sirve como crisol donde deben prender los carbones dormidos usando el rescoldo de un elemental derrotado, demostrando su poder para comunicarse con los destructivos espíritus de la llama y respetarlos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Shaman"]="Every young orc and troll shaman must make the arduous trek up this crag to kindle their spiritual connection with fire and earn their Fire Totem.",["faction:Horde"]="Tucked away in the mountains above Durotar, this isolated shrine preserves ancient elemental rites vital to the spiritual heart of the new Horde."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The path begins along the Southfury River on the southwestern edge of the Southfury Watershed, just northwest of the Valley of Trials. A narrow mountain trail spirals around the peak, leading directly up to the summit.",["al"]={"how to get to shrine of the dormant flame","path to dormant flame","climb dormant flame mountain"},["q"]="How do you reach the Shrine of the Dormant Flame?"},{["a"]="The shrine is a sacred site where aspiring Horde shaman learn to understand and command the element of fire. As part of their Call of Fire journey, initiates must travel to this summit to prepare a ritual draft and kindle the dormant brazier.",["al"]={"shrine of dormant flame purpose","why do shaman go here","call of fire shrine"},["q"]="Why is this shrine important to shaman?"},{["a"]="Telf Joolam is a solitary troll hermit who serves as the keeper of the shrine. He guides young shaman through their trials, concocting a draught of fire to awaken their spiritual sight and testing their resolve.",["al"]={"who is telf joolam","dormant flame npc","shrine keeper"},["q"]="Who is Telf Joolam?"},{["a"]="Shaman who have gathered the required ritual components and defeated a hostile fire elemental place its burning ember into the brazier. This acts as an offering to prove they have the strength and discipline to tame the volatile spirit of flame.",["al"]={"brazier of dormant flame","igniting the flame","shrine brazier quest"},["q"]="What happens when you kindle the brazier?"}},["kw"]={"call of fire","dormant flame","durotar","fire totem","shrine","southfury watershed","telf joolam","valley of trials"},["n"]="Shrine of the Dormant Flame",["s"]="Perched atop the highest peak northwest of the Valley of Trials, the Shrine of the Dormant Flame is a secluded sanctuary revered by Horde shaman. Guided by its solitary keeper, Telf Joolam, initiates make the treacherous climb to commune with the element of fire and prove their spiritual mastery.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Reaching the Shrine of the Dormant Flame requires braving a narrow, winding trail that begins along the Southfury River at the southwestern edge of the Southfury Watershed. High above the red cliffs of Durotar, the mountain summit offers a commanding view of the surrounding lands, though a single misstep along the precipice means certain death. In this quiet refuge wanders Telf Joolam, a solitary hermit tasked with overseeing sacred rites. For aspiring orc and troll shaman undertaking the ritual Call of Fire, the shrine's brazier serves as the crucible where they must ignite slumbering coals using the ember of a vanquished elemental, proving their power to commune with and respect the destructive spirits of flame.",["t"]="A Summit of Trial and Flame"}}}}}
t["subzone:shrine-of-the-fallen-warrior"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="28,327,14.608.0,27.487.0,50.210.0,37.199.0,46.121.0,52.209.0,49.162.0",["h"]="96f9b3",["n"]="Santuario del Guerrero Caído",["s"]="Santuario del Guerrero Caído. Encaramado en una cresta apartada al oeste de El Cruce se encuentra el Santuario del Guerrero Caído, un tranquilo monumento conmemorativo que domina las extensas sabanas rojas de Los Baldíos. Marcado por un plinto de piedra con las iniciales «MK» grabadas y el cuerpo de un guerrero orco caído, está custodiado por la apacible presencia de un Ángel de la Resurrección llamado Koiter. Escondido en lo alto de las colinas al noroeste de El Cruce, el Santuario del Guerrero Caído se alza como un remanso inusualmente solemne en medio del polvo y el peligro de Los Baldíos. Para encontrarlo, los viajeros deben subir por un sendero sinuoso por la cresta al suroeste de la cima hasta alcanzar un suave montículo. En la cima descansa un monumento de piedra tallada, con las iniciales «MK» grabadas en su plinto. Ante él yace la figura en armadura de un guerrero orco en reposo, vigilado día y noche por un Ángel de la Resurrección con nombre propio: Koiter. Aquí no suenan cuernos de batalla, solo reina una tranquila contemplación en honor a un campeón que recorrió las tierras de Kalimdor.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="Warriors of all races often make a quiet pilgrimage to this hill, paying respects to a fallen brother-in-arms who fought bravely before passing into legend.",["faction:Horde"]="Set right in the heartland of Horde territory, this solitary resting place captures the honor, duty, and sacrifice at the core of the shamanic and warrior traditions of Kalimdor."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The shrine sits atop a hill west of the Crossroads in the northern Barrens. Travelers can reach it by locating the base of a ridge southwest of the elevation and following a winding path up to the grassy knoll.",["al"]={"shrine location","where is the shrine","how to get to shrine of fallen warrior"},["q"]="Where is the Shrine of the Fallen Warrior located?"},{["a"]="In-game, he represents a revered fallen warrior. In reality, he is modeled directly after Twincruiser, the orc warrior character played by late Blizzard artist Michel Koiter during early development.",["al"]={"who is the dead orc","fallen warrior identity","twincruiser"},["q"]="Who is the orc lying upon the plinth?"},{["a"]="The runic initials 'MK' honor Michel Koiter, a senior artist who passed away in 2004 during the development of the world.",["al"]={"mk initials","what does mk stand for","letters on the stone"},["q"]="What does the 'MK' carved into the stone mean?"},{["a"]="The Spirit Healer is named Koiter. Unlike ordinary Spirit Healers that only appear to spirits walking in death, Koiter stands in vigil and can be seen clearly by living wanderers who make the trek up the hill.",["al"]={"spirit healer koiter","angel at the shrine","who is the ghost"},["q"]="Who is the Spirit Healer standing beside the shrine?"},{["a"]="No. The Shrine of the Fallen Warrior is not part of any questline or faction conflict. It exists purely as a solemn place of reflection, remembrance, and tribute.",["al"]={"shrine quest","quest for fallen warrior","is there a quest here"},["q"]="Are there any quests associated with this shrine?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","crossroads","koiter","memorial","michel koiter","shrine of the fallen warrior","twincruiser"},["n"]="Shrine of the Fallen Warrior",["s"]="Perched upon a secluded ridge west of the Crossroads lies the Shrine of the Fallen Warrior, a quiet memorial overlooking the sweeping red savannahs of the Barrens. Marked by a stone plinth bearing the initials 'MK' and the body of a fallen orc warrior, it is watched over by the gentle presence of a Spirit Healer named Koiter.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away high upon the hills northwest of the Crossroads, the Shrine of the Fallen Warrior stands as an unusually solemn haven amidst the dust and peril of the Barrens. To find it, travelers must scale a winding ridge pathway southwest of the summit until they reach a gentle mound. Upon the summit rests a carved stone monument, its plinth carved with the initials 'MK'. Before it lies the armored form of an orc warrior at rest, watched over day and night by a named Spirit Healer known as Koiter. There are no battle horns here, only quiet contemplation honoring a champion who walked Kalimdor's lands.",["t"]="A Silent Vigil"},{["b"]="Within the world, the shrine stands as an enduring tribute to a departed champion of the Horde whose soul lingers in the care of the spirits. Outside the realm, the monument serves as a heartfelt tribute created by the game's artists to honor Michel Koiter, a beloved illustrator who passed away during the development of the world. The resting warrior is modeled precisely after Koiter's own beta character, Twincruiser, immortalizing his presence forever beneath Kalimdor's open skies.",["t"]="The Meaning of the Memorial"}}}}}
t["subzone:silver-stream-mine"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,394,31.556.0,20.490.0,52.233.0,32.202.0,42.169.0,46.195.0",["h"]="77d891",["n"]="Mina de Fuenteplata",["s"]="Mina de Fuenteplata. La Mina de Fuenteplata es una mina enana agotada situada en el norte de Loch Modan, resguardada entre la Estación de Algaz y la Presa de las Tres Cabezas. Antaño una rica veta de plata para el reino de Forjaz, el hueco excavado se reconvirtió en un depósito de suministros de la Liga de Mineros antes de ser invadido por alimañas. Hoy en día, los kóbolds Rata de Túnel ocupan los túneles, acumulando equipo robado y raras curiosidades minerales. La Mina de Fuenteplata rebosaba antaño de valioso mineral y contribuyó en gran medida a las reservas de plata de Forjaz. Con el tiempo, los picos de los enanos excavaron lo suficiente como para agotar las vetas principales, convirtiendo las extensas cámaras en un complejo subterráneo vacío. En lugar de abandonar las laboriosas obras de tierra, la Liga de Mineros transformó los pozos en un depósito de almacenamiento seguro para herramientas, cajas de minería y equipo regional. También sirve como la única fuente conocida de las raras Charged Rift Gems, que atraen a arcanistas inquisitivos en busca de delicados componentes de sastrería.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="Apprentice mages journey into the dangerous kobold-infested tunnels specifically to extract Charged Rift Gems, an indispensable ingredient for crafting ritual garments.",["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, Silver Stream Mine is an infuriating loss of hard-earned infrastructure, where clumsy kobolds now sully a respectable Ironforge Miners' League depot."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Originally, it was a productive silver mine excavated by the dwarves of Ironforge. After the veins ran dry, the Ironforge Miners' League repurposed the vacant subterranean halls into a storage depot for tools and excavation supplies.",["al"]={"what is silver stream mine","silver stream history","why was silver stream built"},["q"]="What was the Silver Stream Mine originally used for?"},{["a"]="The mine has been completely overrun by Tunnel Rat kobolds. They chased off the dwarf caretakers and now guard the tunnels, hoarding the League's abandoned supply crates and digging for residual scraps.",["al"]={"who lives in silver stream mine","silver stream mobs","what is inside silver stream mine"},["q"]="Who currently occupies the mine?"},{["a"]="The mine is the only known source of Charged Rift Gems. These volatile, magically reactive stones are sought after by Alliance arcanists to weave potent enchanted robes.",["al"]={"mage quest silver stream","charged rift gems","silver stream mage robes"},["q"]="Why do mages travel to Silver Stream Mine?"},{["a"]="Behind the mine sit broken orcish wagons and ruined catapults, weathered remnants of earlier wartime conflicts that threatened the passages connecting Loch Modan and the northern mountain passes.",["al"]={"orc wagons behind silver stream","broken catapults loch modan mine","horde siege engines loch modan"},["q"]="What are the ruined catapults behind the mine?"}},["kw"]={"charged rift gem","kobold","loch modan","miners league","silver stream mine","tunnel rat"},["n"]="Silver Stream Mine",["s"]="Silver Stream Mine is a depleted dwarf mine located in northern Loch Modan, nestled between Algaz Station and the Stonewrought Dam. Once a rich silver vein for the kingdom of Ironforge, the excavated hollow was repurposed as a Miners' League supply depot before being overrun by vermin. Today, Tunnel Rat kobolds squat inside the tunnels, hoarding stolen equipment and rare mineral curiosities.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Silver Stream Mine once flowed with precious ore, contributing heavily to the silver reserves of Ironforge. In time, the dwarf pickaxes dug deep enough to exhaust the primary veins, turning the sprawling chambers into an empty subterranean complex. Rather than abandon the hard-won earthworks, the Miners' League transformed the shafts into a secure storage depot for tools, mining crates, and regional equipment. It also serves as the only known source of rare Charged Rift Gems, which draw inquisitive arcanists searching for delicate tailoring reagents.",["t"]="From Rich Vein to Storage Depot"},{["b"]="The quiet depot did not remain secure for long. Aggressive Tunnel Rat kobolds, drawn by the smell of unattended tools, candle wax, and forgotten subterranean crevices, swarmed the shafts in large numbers. The Miners' League caretakers were promptly driven out into the Loch Modan cold. Now, the kobolds guard the stolen dwarf crates with manic fervor, while old, shattered orcish catapults and wagons rest forgotten outside the rear entrances, silent reminders of older frontier skirmishes.",["t"]="The Kobold Incursion"}}}}}
t["subzone:silverwind-refuge"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,253,18.477.0,31.191.0,35.107.0,38.147.0",["h"]="1cacba",["n"]="Refugio Brisa de Plata",["s"]="Refugio Brisa de Plata. El Refugio Brisa de Plata es un sereno asentamiento de los elfos de la noche situado en el centro-sur de Vallefresno, justo al norte del Lago Mystral. Protegido por centinelas y elementales de agua aliados, ofrece un acogedor refugio para los viajeros que recorren los senderos boscosos de la espesura. Ubicado entre las plácidas aguas del Lago Mystral y el Lago Iris al norte, el Refugio Brisa de Plata se erige como una de las principales paradas de postas de los elfos de la noche en el centro de Vallefresno, junto a Astranaar. Cuenta con una cómoda posada, artesanos y maestros de profesión que instruyen a los viajeros en herboristería, alquimia, desuello y caza. Custodiado por firmes centinelas junto a espíritus de agua locales, el retiro sirve como un pacífico lugar de descanso para los aliados que atraviesan los umbríos bosques ancestrales.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance wanderers traversing Ashenvale, Silverwind Refuge provides a reliable camp to rest, restock supplies, and refine wilderness trades without venturing all the way to Astranaar.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The refuge serves as a vital stop in Ashenvale for gatherers, offering on-site herbalism training surrounded by the rich flora of Mystral Lake."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Silverwind Refuge is an Alliance settlement, built and maintained by the night elves. It is heavily guarded by the Sentinels, alongside water elementals who help protect the tranquil grounds.",["al"]={"who owns silverwind refuge","is silverwind alliance or horde","who lives at silverwind"},["q"]="Who controls Silverwind Refuge?"},{["a"]="It is located in south-central Ashenvale, positioned directly north of Mystral Lake and south of Iris Lake.",["al"]={"silverwind refuge location","where is silverwind refuge","how to get to silverwind"},["q"]="Where is Silverwind Refuge located?"},{["a"]="Travelers can find an inn, trade supply vendors, and professional trainers offering instruction in herbalism, alchemy, skinning, and hunter skills.",["al"]={"what is at silverwind refuge","silverwind refuge trainers","silverwind vendors"},["q"]="What services are found at the refuge?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","iris lake","mystral lake","night elf","sentinels","silverwind refuge"},["n"]="Silverwind Refuge",["s"]="Silverwind Refuge is a serene night elven settlement nestled in south-central Ashenvale, situated just north of Mystral Lake. Protected by Sentinels and allied water elementals, it offers a welcoming haven for travelers along the forest's wooded trails.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Resting between the placid waters of Mystral Lake and Iris Lake to the north, Silverwind Refuge stands as one of the major night elven waystations in central Ashenvale alongside Astranaar. It boasts a comfortable inn, craftsmen, and wilderness trainers who instruct travelers in herbalism, alchemy, skinning, and hunting. Guarded by stalwart Sentinels alongside local water spirits, the retreat serves as a peaceful rest stop for allies moving through the shaded ancient woods.",["t"]="A Forest Sanctuary"}}}}}
t["subzone:silverwing-grove"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,273,28.504.0,40.250.0,34.116.0,37.228.0,41.159.0",["h"]="01ea2f",["n"]="Claro Ala de Plata",["s"]="Claro Ala de Plata. Escondido en la zona centro-sur de Vallefresno, cerca del Lago Cielo Estrellado, Claro Ala de Plata sirve como punto de concentración para las Centinelas Ala de Plata. Desde esta hondonada fortificada, los guerreros elfos de la noche reúnen a las fuerzas de la Alianza para hacer retroceder a los leñadores del clan Grito de Guerra que arrasan el bosque. Oculto bajo el dosel esmeralda al suroeste de Avanzada Ala de Plata, Claro Ala de Plata es un puesto militar de concentración crucial para las Centinelas Ala de Plata. Lejos de ser un apacible retiro boscoso, funciona como el centro neurálgico de operaciones para la encarnizada disputa territorial de los elfos de la noche contra las talas de la Horda en Garganta Grito de Guerra. Oficiales de alto rango de la Alianza, suministros y exploradores se reúnen aquí, organizando escaramuzas y congregando campeones para defender el ancestral Vallefresno de la expansión de los orcos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The grove is the primary staging ground for Alliance champions seeking to muster and enter the bloody skirmishes of Warsong Gulch.",["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, Silverwing Grove represents the steadfast resolve to halt the desecration of sacred trees at the axes of the Warsong Clan."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Silverwing Grove serves as the staging base for the Silverwing Sentinels. It is where the night elf military and their Alliance allies organize efforts to contest the Warsong Clan's deforesting efforts and enter the ongoing conflict in Warsong Gulch.",["al"]={"why is silverwing grove here","what is silverwing grove","purpose of silverwing grove"},["q"]="What is the purpose of Silverwing Grove?"},{["a"]="It is located in south-central Ashenvale, situated southwest of Silverwing Outpost and just west of Fallen Sky Lake.",["al"]={"silverwing grove location","where is silverwing grove","how to find silverwing grove"},["q"]="Where is Silverwing Grove located?"},{["a"]="The grove is manned by the Silverwing Sentinels alongside Alliance military commanders, including an Alliance Brigadier General, logistical vendors, and officers such as Sentinel Farsong who coordinate efforts against the Horde.",["al"]={"who is at silverwing grove","silverwing grove npcs","who runs silverwing grove"},["q"]="Who operates out of Silverwing Grove?"},{["a"]="No. The grove is an active military post populated by hostile Alliance sentinels and guards who will immediately attack any encroaching Horde members on sight.",["al"]={"is silverwing grove hostile","can horde go to silverwing grove","horde silverwing grove"},["q"]="Can Horde players enter Silverwing Grove?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","fallen sky lake","sentinel farsong","silverwing grove","silverwing sentinels","warsong gulch"},["n"]="Silverwing Grove",["s"]="Tucked away in south-central Ashenvale near Fallen Sky Lake, Silverwing Grove serves as the staging grounds for the Silverwing Sentinels. From this fortified hollow, night elf warriors muster Alliance forces to push back the Warsong Clan loggers tearing through the forest.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Hidden beneath the emerald canopy southwest of Silverwing Outpost, Silverwing Grove is a crucial military staging post for the Silverwing Sentinels. Rather than a tranquil woodland retreat, it functions as the operational heartbeat for the night elves' bitter territorial contest against the Horde's lumber operations in Warsong Gulch. High-ranking Alliance officers, provisions, and scouts gather here, organizing skirmishes and marshaling champions to defend ancient Ashenvale against orcish expansion.",["t"]="Front Line of the Forest War"}}}}}
t["subzone:silverwing-outpost"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,248,21.501.0,18.384.1,36.150.0,32.142.0,55.217.0,33.213.0",["h"]="9d0eaa",["n"]="Avanzada Ala de Plata",["s"]="Avanzada Ala de Plata. La Avanzada Ala de Plata es una guarnición fortificada de elfos de la noche situada en el centro-sur de Vallefresno, al este del Río Falfarren. Comandada por Duriel Moonfire, se erige como el bastión más oriental de la Alianza frente a la Horda en este bosque en disputa. Situada al suroeste del Puesto del Hachazo y justo al norte de la frontera con Los Baldíos, la Avanzada Ala de Plata ocupa una posición estratégica intrínsecamente peligrosa. Al asentarse en la orilla oriental del Río Falfarren —un territorio fuertemente disputado y patrullado por la Horda—, la avanzada sirve como escudo directo para las posesiones de los elfos de la noche en las profundidades del bosque. Duriel Moonfire y sus Centinelas Ala de Plata permanecen bajo el asedio constante de los orcos cercanos, decididos a purgar por completo las fuerzas de los elfos de la noche de la zona.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Silverwing Outpost serves as your vital forward redoubt on the Horde side of the river, checking orc expansion out of Splintertree Post.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, the outpost is an intolerable thorn in the side of Splintertree Post, directly obstructing your movements and supply lines through southern Ashenvale."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It is located in south-central Ashenvale, southwest of Splintertree Post, north of the Barrens border, and on the eastern side of the Falfarren River.",["al"]={"silverwing location","where is silverwing","silverwing outpost map"},["q"]="Where is Silverwing Outpost located?"},{["a"]="The outpost is commanded by Duriel Moonfire, a night elf officer leading the Silverwing Sentinels defending the eastern reaches of the forest.",["al"]={"silverwing leader","who leads silverwing outpost","duriel moonfire"},["q"]="Who commands Silverwing Outpost?"},{["a"]="Silverwing Outpost sits directly on the eastern side of the Falfarren River near Splintertree Post. Its presence allows the Sentinels to cut off Horde supply lines and directly threaten orcish operations in Ashenvale.",["al"]={"why attack silverwing","horde interest in silverwing","splintertree vs silverwing"},["q"]="Why does the Horde target this outpost so aggressively?"},{["a"]="The Silverwing Sentinels are a militant order of night elf warriors and huntresses dedicated to protecting Ashenvale from incursions, particularly against the encroaching lumber camps and war parties of the Horde.",["al"]={"what are silverwings","silverwing sentinels lore","silverwing faction"},["q"]="Who are the Silverwing Sentinels?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","duriel moonfire","falfarren river","silverwing outpost","silverwing sentinels","splintertree post","torek"},["n"]="Silverwing Outpost",["s"]="Silverwing Outpost is a fortified night elf garrison positioned in south-central Ashenvale, east of the Falfarren River. Commanded by Duriel Moonfire, it stands as the easternmost bastion of the Alliance against the Horde in the contested woodland.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated southwest of Splintertree Post and just north of the border with the Barrens, Silverwing Outpost holds an inherently perilous strategic position. By sitting on the eastern side of the Falfarren River—territory heavily contested and patrolled by the Horde—the outpost serves as a direct shield for night elf holdings deeper in the forest. Duriel Moonfire and her Silverwing Sentinels remain under constant siege from nearby orcs determined to purge night elf forces from the area entirely.",["t"]="East of the Falfarren"},{["b"]="The skirmishes surrounding Silverwing Outpost are among the fiercest in Ashenvale. Orcish war parties based out of Splintertree Post, such as raiders led by Torek, launch relentless ambushes against the garrison's walls. For the Horde, neutralizing the outpost is essential to securing the road and expanding resource operations without the constant threat of Sentinel counterattacks.",["t"]="The Constant Front"}}}}}
t["subzone:sishir-canyon"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,352,15.507.0,18.412.0,22.148.0,34.180.0,17.178.0,30.134.0",["h"]="a732d4",["n"]="Cañón Sishir",["s"]="Cañón Sishir. El Cañón Sishir es un escarpado desfiladero en Sierra Espolón, que se abre paso hacia el este a través de las abruptas cumbres. Plagado por densos enjambres de monstruosas arañas Musgoprofundo y cubierto de telarañas, sirve como peligroso acceso a las Ruinas de Eldre'thar. Los viajeros que se atreven a adentrarse en sus enmarañadas profundidades deben enfrentarse a arácnidos venenosos y a su amenazante matriarca. El Cañón Sishir, que nace como una bifurcación de los caminos de montaña de Sierra Espolón, es un traicionero corredor natural que se abre paso hacia las antiguas Ruinas de Eldre'thar. Lejos de ser un apacible sendero de montaña, el desfiladero ha sido completamente invadido por arañas Musgoprofundo. Sus pegajosos mantos de seda y sus cúmulos de sacos de huevos asfixian el suelo pedregoso y las paredes de roca, transformando el barranco en un nido viviente. Los viajeros y centinelas que buscan las ruinas de los elfos de la noche que aguardan más allá deben abrirse camino entre enjambres de agresivas tejedoras.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="The dangerous webbing and venomous Deepmoss spiders make Sishir Canyon a demanding testing ground for hunters tracking and trapping wild beasts in tight ravine quarters.",["race:NightElf"]="The overrun canyon cuts off easy, safe passage to the ancestral Ruins of Eldre'thar, requiring Kaldorei sentinels and scholars to fight through dense spider nests to reach their heritage."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Sishir Canyon is a spider-infested gorge in the Stonetalon Mountains that winds from the main mountain paths toward the ancient Ruins of Eldre'thar.",["al"]={"where is sishir canyon","sishir canyon location"},["q"]="What is Sishir Canyon?"},{["a"]="The canyon is thoroughly claimed by predatory Deepmoss spiders. The arachnids have coated the ravine in dense webbing and egg sacs, preying on anything that enters their territory.",["al"]={"monsters in sishir canyon","spiders in stonetalon canyon"},["q"]="What creatures live in the canyon?"},{["a"]="Besseleth is the formidable spider matriarch dwelling deep within Sishir Canyon. She leads the Deepmoss brood and poses the greatest threat to travelers passing through the area.",["al"]={"besseleth location","giant spider sishir canyon"},["q"]="Who is Besseleth?"},{["a"]="Following the canyon eastward leads directly out to the Ruins of Eldre'thar, an ancient night elven site tucked high in the mountains.",["al"]={"what is at the end of sishir canyon","path through sishir canyon"},["q"]="Where does Sishir Canyon lead?"}},["kw"]={"besseleth","deepmoss","eldre'thar","sishir canyon","spiders","stonetalon","webbing"},["n"]="Sishir Canyon",["s"]="Sishir Canyon is a rugged gorge in the Stonetalon Mountains, carving an eastward path through the craggy heights. Thickly swarmed by monstrous Deepmoss spiders and choked in webbing, it serves as the dangerous approach to the Ruins of Eldre'thar. Travelers who brave its tangled depths must contend with venomous arachnids and their brooding matriarch.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Branching off the mountain roads of the Stonetalon range, Sishir Canyon is a treacherous natural corridor cutting toward the ancient Ruins of Eldre'thar. Rather than a quiet mountain trail, the gorge has been thoroughly overrun by Deepmoss spiders. Their sticky silken sheets and clusters of egg sacs smother the stony ground and rock walls, transforming the ravine into a living nest. Travelers and sentinels seeking the night elven ruins beyond must cut their way through swarms of aggressive webspinners.",["t"]="The Webbed Pass"},{["b"]="Lurking in the deepest recess of the canyon is Besseleth, the massive and deadly matriarch of the Deepmoss brood. Her venom and monstrous size make her a terror to anyone attempting to secure the pass. Local forces in Stonetalon keep a wary watch on the canyon, warning adventurers that venturing into the webbed recesses means facing not just scattered spiders, but an apex predator fiercely guarding her brood.",["t"]="Besseleth's Domain"}}}}}
t["subzone:skittering-dark"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,240,15.324.0,28.197.0,34.159.0,37.117.0",["h"]="1e13b1",["n"]="Penumbra de las Celerácnidas",["s"]="Penumbra de las Celerácnidas. La Penumbra de las Celerácnidas es una mina abandonada y una hondonada boscosa y sombría en el oeste de Bosque de Argénteos. Infestadas por agresivas arañas gigantes, la caverna y los bosques circundantes están repletos de telarañas y peligros para las bestias y los viajeros incautos. Escondida entre las colinas justo al este de la costa occidental de Cala Mareanorte, la Penumbra de las Celerácnidas fue antaño una mina activa. Hoy en día, los pozos están completamente atestados de telarañas y sirven como un extenso nido de arañas gigantes. Con la sombría tejedora Krethis merodeando por el exterior, las arañas cazan a cualquiera que se acerque demasiado.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Horde travelers venturing into Silverpine should take note: the spiders of the Skittering Dark ambush unwary prey that strays from the surrounding woods into their webbed dens."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It is an abandoned mine in western Silverpine Forest that has been entirely overrun by giant spiders. The cavern network and surrounding trees are thick with sticky webbing and predatory arachnids.",["al"]={"skittering dark mine","what is this mine","spider cave silverpine"},["q"]="What is the Skittering Dark?"},{["a"]="No single ruler of the brood is known. The most feared of the spiders is Krethis Shadowspinner, a rare and dangerous weaver that prowls in and around the mine.",["al"]={"spider boss","skittering dark boss","matriarch"},["q"]="Who leads the spiders in the mine?"},{["a"]="It sits nestled against the hills in western Silverpine Forest, just east of the shoreline known as North Tide's Run.",["al"]={"skittering dark location","how to find skittering dark"},["q"]="Where is the Skittering Dark located?"}},["kw"]={"krethis","mine","north tide's run","silverpine","skittering dark","spider"},["n"]="Skittering Dark",["s"]="The Skittering Dark is an abandoned mine and shadowy woodland hollow in western Silverpine Forest. Infested by aggressive giant spiders, the cavern and its surrounding woods are thick with webbing and danger for unwary beasts and travelers.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked into the hills just east of the western coast of North Tide's Run, the Skittering Dark was once a working mine. Today, the shafts are completely choked with cobwebs, serving as the sprawling nest of giant spiders. With the shadowy weaver Krethis haunting the exterior, the spiders hunt anything that strays too close.",["t"]="A Webbed Hollow"}}}}}
t["subzone:skull-rock"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="10,195,17.478.0,19.183.0,24.118.0,40.175.0",["h"]="9a1b6d",["n"]="Roca del Cráneo",["s"]="Roca del Cráneo. Roca del Cráneo es una caverna escondida en los acantilados de la costa oriental de Durotar, justo al este de Orgrimmar. Sirve como un aquelarre fortificado para el culto demoníaco del Filo Ardiente justo delante de las narices de la capital. Oculta bajo los riscos del noreste de Durotar, Roca del Cráneo es uno de los bastiones más peligrosos del culto del Filo Ardiente en la región. Oscuros cultistas, orcos devotos de lo vil y convocadores se reúnen en las profundidades de los serpenteantes túneles para practicar artes demoníacas y urdir conspiraciones contra la naciente Horda. La célula está liderada por el peligroso brujo Gazz'uz, cuyas operaciones representan una amenaza inminente para las cercanas Puertas de Orgrimmar y los viajeros que recorren la costa este.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warlock"]="The dark arts practiced within Skull Rock showcase the unchecked spread of demonic influence that Thrall's Horde seeks to root out and control.",["faction:Horde"]="Clearing the cultists from Skull Rock is vital to securing the coastal approaches to Durotar and protecting Orgrimmar from subversion from within."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Skull Rock is a cave system situated in northeastern Durotar along the coast. It is occupied by cultists of the Burning Blade who use its natural cover to plot against Thrall's Horde.",["al"]={"skull rock cave","where is skull rock","what is in skull rock"},["q"]="What is Skull Rock?"},{["a"]="The cavern is infested by the Burning Blade cult, led by the orc warlock Gazz'uz from the deepest chamber of the cave.",["al"]={"who leads skull rock","who runs skull rock","skull rock boss"},["q"]="Who controls Skull Rock?"},{["a"]="Its proximity to Orgrimmar makes it a severe security hazard. The Burning Blade actively seeks to undermine Thrall's new realm and plunge the orcs back into demonic servitude.",["al"]={"why clear skull rock","why is skull rock dangerous"},["q"]="Why does the Horde care about this cave?"}},["kw"]={"burning blade","cultists","durotar","gazz'uz","orgrimmar","skull rock"},["n"]="Skull Rock",["s"]="Skull Rock is a cavern tucked into the eastern coastal cliffs of Durotar, just east of Orgrimmar. It serves as a fortified coven for the demonic Burning Blade cult right under the capital's nose.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Hidden beneath the crags of northeastern Durotar, Skull Rock is one of the most perilous strongholds of the Burning Blade cult in the region. Dark cultists, fel-worshipping orcs, and summoners gather deep within the winding tunnels to practice demonic arts and weave conspiracies against the nascent Horde. The cell is led by the dangerous warlock Gazz'uz, whose operations pose an imminent threat to the nearby gates of Orgrimmar and travelers traversing the eastern shoreline.",["t"]="A Den of Cultists"}}}}}
t["subzone:sludge-fen"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="10,379,22.621.0,31.676.1,60.247.0,37.207.0,65.258.0,46.226.0",["h"]="b7ecfc",["n"]="El Fangal",["s"]="El Fangal. El Fangal es un campo petrolífero industrial y tóxico explotado por Ventura y Cía. en el noreste de Los Baldíos. Antaño un estanque prístino de aguas de color azul cristalino, el humedal quedó transformado en un lodazal aceitoso después de que los goblins levantaran plataformas de perforación y maquinaria. La explotación está supervisada por Supervisor Lugwizzle y atrae un constante espionaje industrial y sabotajes por parte de sus rivales en Trinquete. Antes de la llegada de Ventura y Cía., El Fangal era un estanque virgen de aguas cristalinas alimentado por manantiales naturales en los áridos Baldíos. Impulsada por la implacable búsqueda de beneficios, Ventura y Cía. construyó una extensa explotación de extracción petrolífera sobre la cuenca, arruinando el humedal y convirtiéndolo en un embalse repleto de fango cubierto de densos residuos industriales. Bajo la mirada de Supervisor Lugwizzle, perforadores, ingenieros y capataces goblin bombean crudo a todas horas, sin importarles la ruina medioambiental. Sus aguas están ahora densas por los vertidos y los subproductos tóxicos, dejando a la fauna acuática autóctona asfixiada bajo la grasa.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Sludge Fen stands as a sickening testament to unnatural exploitation. Horde druids journey into its oily depths during the Trial of the Sea Lion to retrieve the Half Pendant of Aquatic Agility.",["profession:Engineering"]="The Venture Company operates cutting-edge shredders and machinery here, making the site an irresistible target for blueprints, specialized components, and trade theft orchestrated from Ratchet."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Sludge Fen was originally a basin of pure, crystal-blue water. The Venture Company ruined the natural oasis when they built an oil rig and refining operation directly on top of it, drowning the surrounding wetland in crude oil and chemical refuse.",["al"]={"sludge fen past","was sludge fen always polluted","sludge fen history"},["q"]="What was Sludge Fen like before the Venture Company arrived?"},{["a"]="The oil field is run by Supervisor Lugwizzle on behalf of the Venture Company. He oversees the labor force of overseers, drillers, and engineers alongside lieutenants like Overseer Glibby and Foreman Grills.",["al"]={"sludge fen boss","who leads sludge fen","supervisor lugwizzle"},["q"]="Who runs the operation at Sludge Fen?"},{["a"]="The goblin Wizzlecrank was sent by Sputtervalve from Ratchet to steal the Venture Company's superior shredder design. However, he leaped into the cockpit without first securing the ignition key, leaving him stranded surrounded by hostile Venture Co. workers.",["al"]={"wizzlecrank shredder","goblin in shredder sludge fen","why is shredder stuck"},["q"]="Why is there a hijacked shredder parked in the middle of the fen?"},{["a"]="Horde druids undergoing the Trial of the Sea Lion are guided to the bottom of the contaminated pool to recover the Half Pendant of Aquatic Agility from a submerged lockbox, testing their endurance against the foul environment.",["al"]={"druid quest sludge fen","aquatic agility half pendant","aquatic form trial"},["q"]="Why do druids dive into these polluted waters?"}},["kw"]={"oil rig","shredder","sludge fen","sputtervalve","supervisor lugwizzle","the barrens","venture co","wizzlecrank"},["n"]="Sludge Fen",["s"]="Sludge Fen is a toxic industrial oil field operated by the Venture Company in the northeastern Barrens. Once a pristine, crystal-blue pool, the wetland was transformed into an oily quagmire after the goblins erected drilling platforms and machinery. The operation is overseen by Supervisor Lugwizzle and attracts constant industrial espionage and sabotage from rivals in Ratchet.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the arrival of the Venture Company, Sludge Fen was an untainted pool of crystal-clear water fed by natural springs in the arid Barrens. Driven by the relentless pursuit of profit, the Venture Company constructed an extensive oil-drilling operation over the basin, despoiling the wetland into a sludge-filled reservoir coated in heavy industrial waste. Overseen by Supervisor Lugwizzle, goblin drillers, engineers, and overseers pump crude oil around the clock, heedless of the environmental ruin. The waters are now thick with runoff and toxic byproducts, leaving the native aquatic life choked beneath the grease.",["t"]="Industrial Devastation"},{["b"]="The fen's machinery and shredder innovations have made it a prime target for industrial theft. In nearby Ratchet, Tinkers' Union engineer Sputtervalve has faced fierce pressure to match the Venture Company's cutting-edge logging and excavation technology. Rather than inventing his own designs, Sputtervalve dispatched an operative named Wizzlecrank to commandeer a Venture Company shredder straight from the Sludge Fen. Because Wizzlecrank foolishly hijacked the machine without securing the ignition key, hired mercenaries are often drawn into the mire to pry the keys from Lugwizzle and escort the stolen war machine out through a gauntlet of furious Venture Co. employees.",["t"]="Corporate Rivalry and Espionage"}}}}}
t["subzone:solliden-farmstead"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,295,17.511.0,21.395.0,55.257.0,57.315.0,58.243.0,58.238.0",["h"]="e5220f",["n"]="Hacienda Solliden",["s"]="Hacienda Solliden. La Hacienda Solliden es una granja de calabazas humana activa situada en el oeste de los Claros de Tirisfal, justo al norte de Camposanto. Representa una rara anomalía en el norte de Lordaeron: granjeros nativos vivos que sobrevivieron a la Plaga de la no-muerte y se aferran ferozmente a su tierra bajo la sombra de la Cruzada Escarlata. Mientras la mayor parte de Lordaeron caía en la ruina y la podredumbre, los campos de la Hacienda Solliden aún producen cosechas sanas. El asentamiento se remonta siglos atrás, cuando familias nobles inmigrantes de Strom adquirieron parcelas de pioneros por todo Tirisfal. En la actualidad, estos granjeros humanos supervivientes viven bajo la atenta protección de la Cruzada Escarlata, que patrulla desde una torre cercana. Traumatizados y aislados, defienden su hacienda con una hostilidad inquebrantable, atacando a cualquier forastero que se acerque, ya sea de la Horda o de la Alianza.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Seeing living humans tilling Lordaeron's soil brings a glimmer of hope, but the bitter reality is that these isolated survivors view Stormwind's citizens with the same xenophobic hatred they hold for the undead.",["race:Undead"]="For the newly risen Forsaken, Solliden Farmstead is an immediate lesson in realpolitik: living Lordaeronians who despise what you have become, serving as both raw material for Apothecary toxins and a potential southern beachhead."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Solliden farmers are native Lordaeron humans who miraculously escaped infection during the Third War. Shielded by the Scarlet Crusade patrolling from a nearby tower, they stubbornly continue cultivating the land rather than fleeing their ancestral home.",["al"]={"why are they alive","who are these farmers","living humans in tirisfal"},["q"]="Why are there living humans farming in Tirisfal Glades?"},{["a"]="Living through the fall of Lordaeron has left the farmers paranoid, bitter, and completely untrusting of anyone outside their immediate circle. Protected by the fanatical Scarlet Crusade, they view all trespassers as potential threats or infected scavengers, attacking Alliance and Horde travelers indiscriminately.",["al"]={"why do farmers attack alliance","are they alliance","why red to alliance"},["q"]="Why are the Solliden farmers hostile to Alliance players?"},{["a"]="Apothecaries serving the Royal Apothecary Society require fresh, uncorrupted organic matter to test and refine their New Plague. The plump, untainted pumpkins growing in Solliden's soil serve as ideal living hosts for developing toxic strains.",["al"]={"why steal pumpkins","fields of grief pumpkin quest","royal apothecary society pumpkins"},["q"]="Why do the Forsaken want pumpkins from Solliden Farmstead?"},{["a"]="Deathguard Simmer is a Forsaken officer stationed near Deathknell. He sends fledgling Forsaken to raid the farm, steal ten of its pumpkins for Apothecary Johaan in Brill, and teach the humans and their Scarlet Crusade protectors a lesson.",["al"]={"why kill the farmers","deathguard simmer quest","reaping the reapers"},["q"]="Who is Deathguard Simmer, and why does he target the farm?"}},["kw"]={"deathguard simmer","deathknell","fields of grief","pumpkins","solliden","solliden farmstead","tirisfal glades"},["n"]="Solliden Farmstead",["s"]="Solliden Farmstead is an active human pumpkin farm nestled in western Tirisfal Glades, just north of Deathknell. It represents a rare anomaly in northern Lordaeron: living native farmers who survived the Plague of Undeath and cling fiercely to their soil under the shadow of the Scarlet Crusade.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While most of Lordaeron fell to ruin and rot, the fields of Solliden Farmstead still produce healthy crops. The settlement traces its lineage back centuries to when immigrant noble families from Strom acquired pioneer plots across Tirisfal. Today, these surviving human farmers live under the watchful shield of the Scarlet Crusade patrolling from a nearby tower. Traumatized and insular, they defend their homestead with unyielding hostility, striking at any outsiders who draw near—Horde and Alliance alike.",["t"]="A Defiant Remnant"},{["b"]="To the Forsaken just emerging from Deathknell, Solliden is both a threat and a resource. The Royal Apothecary Society eyes the farm's pristine pumpkins as prime organic testing material for brewing their New Plague. Meanwhile, Forsaken officers like Deathguard Simmer send fledgling recruits to raid the fields, steal those pumpkins for Apothecary Johaan in Brill, and teach the living a lesson.",["t"]="Eyes in the Undercity"}}}}}
t["subzone:south-gate-outpost"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,291,29.544.0,42.228.0,57.255.0,52.251.0",["h"]="06f919",["n"]="Avanzada de la Puerta Sur",["s"]="Avanzada de la Puerta Sur. La Avanzada de la Puerta Sur es un puesto de montaña enano fortificado situado a lo largo del Paso de la Puerta Sur, entre Dun Morogh y Loch Modan. Custodiando el nevado camino del sur, sus montaraces protegen el constante flujo de viajeros que transitan entre las gélidas alturas de Forjaz y el valle templado de Loch Modan. Encaramada a medio camino en el desfiladero de alta montaña del Paso de la Puerta Sur, la Avanzada de la Puerta Sur marca la frontera entre las laderas nevadas de Dun Morogh y la verde cuenca de Loch Modan. Aquí están apostados montaraces de Forjaz encargados de patrullar las curvas rocosas y mantener a la fauna peligrosa lejos del camino principal. En comparación con sus apurados camaradas de la Avanzada de la Puerta Norte, los defensores de este puesto han asegurado en gran medida su tramo de camino, permitiendo que viajeros, peregrinos y carros de comercio con destino a Thelsamar viajen con relativa seguridad.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The outpost serves as a dependable military shelter along one of Khaz Modan's primary domestic supply lines, keeping the passage between the capital and eastern settlements open.",["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves leaving Coldridge Valley and Dun Morogh for the first time, South Gate Outpost is the final chilly landmark before descending into the vibrant, sunlit lands of Loch Modan."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It serves as a fortified border checkpoint and garrison along South Gate Pass. Mountaineers stationed here keep the snowy transit road clear of mountain beasts and hostile interlopers traveling between Dun Morogh and Loch Modan.",["al"]={"why is south gate outpost here","south gate outpost purpose","what is south gate outpost"},["q"]="What is the purpose of South Gate Outpost?"},{["a"]="The garrison at South Gate Outpost has successfully culled the aggressive wildlife immediately bordering the road. North Gate Outpost, by contrast, contends with heavier incursions and wilder mountain terrain, leaving the southern pass comparatively calm.",["al"]={"difference between north gate and south gate","is south gate safe","south gate vs north gate"},["q"]="Why is it so much calmer here than at North Gate Outpost?"},{["a"]="Heading westward up the pass brings you into the snowy highlands of Dun Morogh toward Ironforge. Traveling eastward downhill leads directly out into the temperate valley of Loch Modan, with the road winding straight toward the settlement of Thelsamar.",["al"]={"where does this road go","south gate road destination","south gate pass path"},["q"]="Where does the road through South Gate Outpost lead?"}},["kw"]={"dun morogh","dwarf","ironforge road","loch modan","mountaineers","south gate outpost","south gate pass","thelsamar"},["n"]="South Gate Outpost",["s"]="South Gate Outpost is a fortified dwarven mountain post situated along the South Gate Pass between Dun Morogh and Loch Modan. Manning the snowy southern road, its mountaineers guard the steady flow of travelers walking between Ironforge's frigid heights and the temperate valley of the Loch.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched midway through the high mountain cut of South Gate Pass, South Gate Outpost marks the frontier between the snowy slopes of Dun Morogh and the verdant basin of Loch Modan. Stationed here are Ironforge mountaineers tasked with patrolling the rocky switchbacks and keeping dangerous wildlife off the main highway. Compared to their hard-pressed kin up at North Gate Outpost, the defenders here have largely secured their stretch of road, allowing travelers, pilgrims, and trade wagons headed toward Thelsamar to journey in relative safety.",["t"]="Watchers of the Southern Road"}}}}}
t["subzone:south-gate-pass"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,259,13.416.0,19.325.0,32.214.0,34.211.0,48.220.0",["h"]="998093",["n"]="Paso de la Puerta Sur",["s"]="Paso de la Puerta Sur. El Paso de la Puerta Sur es la principal vía montañosa que une las nevadas alturas de Dun Morogh con la cuenca del valle de Loch Modan. Flanqueado por túneles y puestos de vigilancia enanos, sirve como la ruta más directa entre Forjaz y el asentamiento de Thelsamar. Esculpido a través de la cordillera de Khaz Modan, el Paso de la Puerta Sur conecta las altas montañas de Dun Morogh con el ondulado valle de Loch Modan hacia el este. Los viajeros que dejan atrás las frías laderas emergen a través de arcos de piedra hacia las tierras centrales enanas, más cálidas. Dado que el camino conduce directamente hacia Thelsamar, soporta un flujo constante de montañeros, mensajeros y aventureros recién instruidos que parten de la capital.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The pass serves as a vital internal artery connecting Ironforge with the eastern Alliance territories, maintained and secured by the King's Mountaineers.",["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves leaving Dun Morogh, South Gate Pass is the threshold where the icy mountain air gives way to the open valleys and quarries of Loch Modan."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Heading west through the tunnels brings you into the snowy highlands of Dun Morogh, on the road toward Ironforge. Traveling east leads down into the basin of Loch Modan, directly toward the settlement of Thelsamar.",["al"]={"where does south gate pass go","south gate pass destination","south gate road"},["q"]="Where does South Gate Pass lead?"},{["a"]="The road itself is relatively secure thanks to the dwarven guards stationed at South Gate Outpost, but bears, spiders, and encroaching troggs inhabit the surrounding crags and hillsides outside the tunnel mouth.",["al"]={"is south gate pass dangerous","south gate pass threats"},["q"]="Is South Gate Pass safe to travel?"},{["a"]="South Gate Pass provides the most direct and convenient overland connection between Dun Morogh and Thelsamar, making it the preferred route for local trade, supply caravans, and travelers heading into central Loch Modan.",["al"]={"south gate vs north gate","why use south gate"},["q"]="Why is this pass used more than North Gate Pass?"}},["kw"]={"dun morogh","loch modan","mountaineers","south gate outpost","south gate pass","thelsamar","tunnel"},["n"]="South Gate Pass",["s"]="South Gate Pass is the primary mountain thoroughfare linking the snowy heights of Dun Morogh with the valley basin of Loch Modan. Flanked by dwarven tunnels and watch posts, it serves as the most direct route between Ironforge and the settlement of Thelsamar.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Carved straight through the Khaz Modan range, South Gate Pass connects Dun Morogh's high mountains to the rolling valley of Loch Modan to the east. Travelers leaving the cold slopes behind emerge through stone archways into the warmer dwarven heartlands. Because the path leads straight toward Thelsamar, it carries a steady flow of mountaineers, couriers, and newly trained adventurers setting out from the capital.",["t"]="The Road East"},{["b"]="The pass is fortified against wild beasts and prowling troggs by the South Gate Outpost, where dwarven mountaineers maintain a constant watch. Though generally safer than the untamed wilds deeper in the valley, travelers are advised to keep to the road, as hostile wildlife and roving threats frequently probe the approaches.",["t"]="A Guarded Threshold"}}}}}
t["subzone:south-tide-s-run"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,238,17.353.0,34.119.0,55.234.0,49.159.0",["h"]="7787a1",["n"]="Cala Mareasur",["s"]="Cala Mareasur. Cala Mareasur es la solitaria costa suroccidental de Bosque de Argénteos, extendiéndose a lo largo de las frías aguas del Mare Magnum. Flanqueando el interior boscoso, estas arenas húmedas y su oleaje actúan como el homólogo meridional de Cala Mareanorte. Extendiéndose por el extremo suroccidental de Bosque de Argénteos, Cala Mareasur conforma un límite desolado entre los bosques y el Mare Magnum. A diferencia de los protegidos caminos orientales que descienden hacia La Muralla de Cringrís, esta costa abierta sufre el embate directo de las mareas occidentales, sirviendo como un inhóspito páramo costero prácticamente inexplorado por los asentamientos del interior.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Undead"]="The wild southwestern coast lies far from the protection of the Sepulcher, making it an empty frontier rarely trodden by the Forsaken."},["faq"]={{["a"]="South Tide's Run occupies the southwestern coastline of Silverpine Forest, bordering the open expanse of the Great Sea.",["al"]={"where is south tides run","south tides run location","south tide run map"},["q"]="Where is South Tide's Run located?"},{["a"]="Both are long stretches of beach defining Silverpine Forest's western shoreline, but South Tide's Run covers the southern portion of the coast, whereas North Tide's Run extends along the northwest near the border with Tirisfal Glades.",["al"]={"north tides run vs south tides run","difference between tide runs"},["q"]="How does South Tide's Run differ from North Tide's Run?"},{["a"]="There are no major towns or outposts along the beach itself. Most Forsaken activity remains inland near the main thoroughfares, leaving the shoreline isolated.",["al"]={"towns in south tides run","who lives in south tides run"},["q"]="Are there any settlements along South Tide's Run?"}},["kw"]={"great sea","silverpine coast","silverpine forest","south tide's run","south tides run"},["n"]="South Tide's Run",["s"]="South Tide's Run is the lonely southwestern coastline of Silverpine Forest, stretching along the cold waters of the Great Sea. Flanking the forested interior, these damp sands and surf serve as the southern complement to North Tide's Run.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Stretching along the southwestern edge of Silverpine Forest, South Tide's Run forms a desolate boundary between the woods and the Great Sea. Unlike the protected eastern roads that lead down toward the Greymane Wall, this open shore takes the brunt of the western tides, serving as a bleak coastal wilderness largely untouched by the settlements inland.",["t"]="The Western Shore"}}}}}
t["subzone:southern-gold-road"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,301,19.606.0,29.443.0,48.191.0,31.158.0,72.228.0,39.226.0",["h"]="43e1dc",["n"]="Camino del Oro Sur",["s"]="Camino del Oro Sur. El Camino del Oro Sur es la vía desértica vital que se extiende a través de la mitad sur de Los Baldíos, uniendo las llanuras centrales con El Gran Elevador. Sirve como una arteria indispensable para el comercio regional, transportando caravanas, suministros y caminantes que viajan entre confines lejanos de Kalimdor. Comenzando oficialmente en el puente de piedra que divide las mitades norte y sur de Los Baldíos, el Camino del Oro Sur discurre directamente hacia el sur hasta encontrarse con El Gran Elevador, que desciende hacia Las Mil Agujas. Al igual que el tramo norte, llamado sencillamente Camino del Oro, esta polvorienta calzada debe su apelativo al interminable flujo de lucrativas caravanas mercantes que la recorren de punta a punta. A pesar del constante hostigamiento de las tribus locales de jabaespines y de los depredadores que merodean por la sabana, sigue siendo una de las rutas de larga distancia más transitadas del continente, transportando mercancías entre puestos avanzados remotos y puertos bulliciosos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="The road serves as the backbone of Horde supply lines running between the central crossway of the Barrens and the southern outposts nearing Thousand Needles."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The road officially begins at the bridge that splits the northern and southern halves of the Barrens, continuing southward until it reaches the edge of the Thousand Needles at the Great Lift.",["al"]={"southern gold road path","southern gold road route","where is southern gold road"},["q"]="Where does the Southern Gold Road start and end?"},{["a"]="The thoroughfare is named for the valuable trade caravans that regularly travel along it, ferrying precious goods, ore, and coin across the heart of Kalimdor.",["al"]={"why called gold road","gold road name origin","gold road meaning"},["q"]="Why is it called the Gold Road?"},{["a"]="The dividing line is the bridge crossing the central divide of the Barrens. North of that point, the trail is known simply as the Gold Road, while the stretch leading south to the Great Lift is designated the Southern Gold Road.",["al"]={"gold road vs southern gold road","two gold roads"},["q"]="What is the difference between the Gold Road and the Southern Gold Road?"},{["a"]="Aside from local Horde couriers and patrols, merchants and explorers make use of the route to travel between distant territories, connecting places like Gadgetzan to the far south with Darkshore and Moonglade in the far north.",["al"]={"who uses southern gold road","caravans southern gold road"},["q"]="Who travels along this stretch of road?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","caravans","gold road","great lift","southern gold road","thousand needles"},["n"]="Southern Gold Road",["s"]="The Southern Gold Road is the vital desert thoroughfare stretching through the southern half of the Barrens, linking the central plains to the Great Lift. It serves as an indispensable artery for regional trade, carrying caravans, supplies, and wayfarers traveling between distant reaches of Kalimdor.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Officially beginning at the stone bridge dividing the northern and southern halves of the Barrens, the Southern Gold Road runs directly south until it meets the Great Lift leading down into the Thousand Needles. Like the northern portion simply named the Gold Road, this dusty highway derives its moniker from the endless stream of lucrative merchant caravans that trek along its length. Despite constant harassment from local quilboar tribes and predators prowling the savannah, it remains one of the busiest long-distance paths on the continent, ferrying goods between remote outposts and bustling ports.",["t"]="Artery of the South"},{["b"]="The road sees travel far beyond local Horde traffic. Adventurers and hardy traders journeying to and from places as far-flung as Gadgetzan in the southern deserts of Tanaris, Auberdine along the misty shores of Darkshore, and the sacred groves of Nighthaven in Moonglade tread this sun-baked expanse. For travelers journeying on foot through Kalimdor's interior, surviving the journey down the Southern Gold Road is a grueling rite of passage.",["t"]="A Crossroads of Distant Lands"}}}}}
t["subzone:southshore"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="10,321,21.528.0,22.451.0,70.248.0,70.235.0,33.201.0,58.183.0",["h"]="d1ad4d",["n"]="Costasur",["s"]="Costasur. Costasur es un puerto costero humano en las Laderas de Trabalomas y uno de los pocos bastiones supervivientes de la Alianza en la caída Lordaeron. Antaño una apacible aldea de pescadores, ahora se erige como un asediado bastión que se enfrenta a la hostilidad constante de la guarnición de los Renegados en Molino Tarren, de bandidos rebeldes de la Hermandad y de monstruos de la costa. Costasur cobró importancia por primera vez durante la Primera Guerra, cuando los barcos de refugiados que transportaban a supervivientes del caído reino de Ventormenta desembarcaron en sus playas. Aunque fue disputada e invadida durante la Segunda Guerra, fue reconstruida y más tarde soportó los horrores de la Tercera Guerra. Hoy en día, mientras el resto de Lordaeron yace en ruinas o bajo el dominio de los Renegados, Costasur se mantiene firmemente leal a la Gran Alianza. Ofrece refugio a supervivientes humanos desplazados, paladines veteranos de la Mano de Plata y eruditos del Kirin Tor.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Southshore serves as your primary haven, quest hub, and military redoubt in northern Lordaeron, offering essential support against both the Forsaken and the Syndicate.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde—especially the Forsaken at nearby Tarren Mill—Southshore represents an obstinate Alliance enclave trespassing on land reclaimed by the dead."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Southshore was spared total destruction during the Scourge's invasion. Its surviving human populace reaffirmed their historic oaths to the Grand Alliance, receiving military and logistical backing from Stormwind to maintain a foothold in the north.",["al"]={"why is southshore alliance","who controls southshore","southshore alliance lordaeron"},["q"]="Why is Southshore still aligned with the Alliance when Lordaeron fell?"},{["a"]="Tarren Mill is held by the Forsaken, while Southshore is the primary Alliance bastion in the region. Both factions claim rightful dominion over the Hillsbrad Foothills, resulting in near-constant border skirmishes, raids, and sabotage.",["al"]={"southshore tarren mill war","why do southshore and tarren mill fight","hillsbrad conflict"},["q"]="Why is there such intense fighting between Southshore and Tarren Mill?"},{["a"]="Civil governance is handled by Magistrate Henry Maleb, who took over after the previous magistrate was assassinated by the Syndicate. Military defense and town security are directed by Marshal Redpath.",["al"]={"southshore leader","who runs southshore","magistrate maleb"},["q"]="Who leads the town of Southshore?"},{["a"]="Beyond the Forsaken, Southshore must fend off coastal murlocs and naga, Crushridge ogres descending from the Alterac Mountains, and the criminal Syndicate based out of Durnholde Keep.",["al"]={"southshore enemies","threats to southshore"},["q"]="What threats does Southshore face other than the Forsaken?"}},["kw"]={"hillsbrad","jessen","lordaeron","maleb","redpath","southshore","syndicate","tarren mill"},["n"]="Southshore",["s"]="Southshore is a coastal human port in the Hillsbrad Foothills and one of the Alliance's few surviving strongholds in fallen Lordaeron. Once a sleepy fishing village, it now stands as an embattled bastion facing constant hostility from the Forsaken garrison at Tarren Mill, rogue Syndicate bandits, and shoreline monsters.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Southshore first rose to prominence during the First War when refugee boats carrying survivors from the fallen kingdom of Stormwind landed upon its beaches. Though contested and overrun during the Second War, it was rebuilt and later endured the horrors of the Third War. Today, while the rest of Lordaeron lies in ruins or under the rule of the Forsaken, Southshore remains fiercely loyal to the Grand Alliance. It offers shelter to displaced human survivors, veteran paladins of the Silver Hand, and scholars of the Kirin Tor.",["t"]="A Beacon in Lordaeron"},{["b"]="Despite its scenic docks and famous turtle bisque, life in Southshore is perilous. Led by Magistrate Henry Maleb and Marshal Redpath, the town struggles against relentless pressure. To the north, the Forsaken of Tarren Mill wage a bitter border conflict for dominance over Hillsbrad. Inland, the aristocratic outlaws of the Syndicate raid supply lines and assassinate local leaders, while ogres, murlocs, and naga constantly harass the town's borders.",["t"]="Besieged on All Fronts"}}}}}
t["subzone:spirit-rise"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="11,286,26.464.0,19.201.0,30.207.0,51.151.0,39.181.0",["h"]="a07d27",["n"]="Alto de los Espíritus",["s"]="Alto de los Espíritus. El Alto de los Espíritus es la meseta noroccidental de Cima del Trueno y sirve como el principal santuario de la capital tauren para el estudio espiritual y chamánico. Supervisado por guías espirituales como la tribu Skychaser, cuenta con salas de entrenamiento sagradas en la superficie y desciende hacia las cavernosas Pozas de las Visiones en las profundidades. Encaramado en lo alto de los riscos que dominan las llanuras de Mulgore, el Alto de los Espíritus está dedicado a la comunión con los elementos y los espíritus de los ancestros. Conectado a la meseta central mediante puentes de cuerda, alberga la Sala de los Espíritus y el pabellón de Sanación Espiritual, donde chamanes novatos y veteranos se reúnen para profundizar su conexión con la tierra, el aire, el fuego y el agua. La tribu Skychaser mantiene una fuerte presencia por todo el alto, guiando a quienes buscan respuestas a través de tradiciones ancestrales.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Shaman"]="For shaman of the Horde, Spirit Rise serves as an essential gathering place to consult trainers, perform elemental rites, and commune with ancestral spirits.",["race:Tauren"]="The rise embodies the deep spiritual roots of your people, offering solace away from secular duties alongside the mystical waters of the Pools of Vision."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Spirit Rise is the spiritual heart of Thunder Bluff, primarily dedicated to shamanic practice, healing, and communing with nature spirits and ancestors. It also serves as the entryway to the Pools of Vision.",["al"]={"what is spirit rise","spirit rise purpose","why visit spirit rise"},["q"]="What is Spirit Rise known for?"},{["a"]="The Skychaser tribe holds prominent influence here, fostering the spiritual traditions, divination rituals, and shamanic training that define the rise.",["al"]={"who runs spirit rise","spirit rise tribe","skychaser tribe"},["q"]="Which tauren tribe leads activities on Spirit Rise?"},{["a"]="A descent through the rise leads into the Pools of Vision, a humid subterranean cavern filled with steaming waters where seers and spiritual practitioners meditate and seek visions.",["al"]={"spirit rise cave","below spirit rise","pools of vision entrance"},["q"]="What can I find underneath Spirit Rise?"}},["kw"]={"hall of spirits","mulgore","pools of vision","shaman","skychaser","spirit rise","thunder bluff"},["n"]="Spirit Rise",["s"]="Spirit Rise is the northwest mesa of Thunder Bluff, serving as the tauren capital's premier sanctum for spiritual and shamanic study. Overseen by spiritual guides such as the Skychaser tribe, it features sacred training halls above and descends into the cavernous Pools of Vision below.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched high upon the bluffs overlooking the plains of Mulgore, Spirit Rise is devoted to communion with the elements and ancestor spirits. Connected to the central mesa by rope bridges, it houses the Hall of Spirits and the Spiritual Healing pavilion, where young and veteran shaman gather to deepen their connection with the earth, air, fire, and water. The Skychaser tribe maintains a strong presence across the rise, guiding seekers through ancient traditions.",["t"]="A Sanctuary of the Spirits"},{["b"]="Beneath the breezy huts and open-air totem shrines lies an entrance burrowing into the mesa itself: the steamy Pools of Vision, a sacred subterranean cavern where seers peer into spirit-touched waters.",["t"]="Caves and Crossings"}}}}}
t["subzone:spirit-rock"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="11,255,27.445.0,29.236.0,29.217.0,16.204.0",["h"]="af69be",["n"]="Roca de los Espíritus",["s"]="Roca de los Espíritus. La Roca de los Espíritus es un risco sagrado situado en los escarpados riscos sobre el Valle de los Retos, en Durotar. Accesible a través de un sendero serpenteante conocido como el Sendero Oculto, sirve como un lugar sagrado y apartado donde los iniciados comunican directamente con las fuerzas elementales de la tierra. Con vistas al cañón rojo donde los jóvenes guerreros y exploradores de la Horda comienzan su adiestramiento, la Roca de los Espíritus se erige como un altar de comunión. Aislada del estrépito del Valle de los Retos, solo se puede acceder a ella a través del Sendero Oculto que serpentea por la cresta rocosa. Los aspirantes a chamán peregrinan a este desolado promontorio para beber el tradicional sapta, descubriendo el misterio del mundo físico para escuchar los retumbos y susurros de la propia tierra.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Shaman"]="Spirit Rock is a vital rite of passage for young orc and troll shaman, who venture up the Hidden Path to drink the Earth Sapta and forge their first bond with the spirits of stone and soil."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Spirit Rock is a sacred site used primarily by Horde shaman initiates. By consuming a specialized draught known as an Earth Sapta at the rock, novices gain the spiritual vision required to commune directly with the spirits of the earth.",["al"]={"spirit rock purpose","what happens at spirit rock","spirit rock use"},["q"]="What is Spirit Rock used for?"},{["a"]="Spirit Rock sits high in the cliffs above the Valley of Trials in southwestern Durotar. It is accessible by ascending the Hidden Path, a narrow, unmarked trail that winds out of the canyon floor into the rugged hills.",["al"]={"how to get to spirit rock","path to spirit rock","spirit rock location"},["q"]="How do you reach Spirit Rock?"},{["a"]="A sapta is a ceremonial elemental brew prepared by shaman trainers. Drinking it alters the seeker's perception, allowing them to perceive elemental manifestations that remain invisible to ordinary senses.",["al"]={"earth sapta","what is sapta","sapta drink"},["q"]="What is a sapta?"}},["kw"]={"call of earth","durotar","earth spirits","hidden path","sapta","shaman","spirit rock","valley of trials"},["n"]="Spirit Rock",["s"]="Spirit Rock is a sacred crag perched in the rugged bluffs above the Valley of Trials in Durotar. Reached by a winding trail known as the Hidden Path, it serves as a secluded holy site where initiates commune directly with the elemental forces of the land.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Overlooking the red canyon where young Horde warriors and scouts begin their training, Spirit Rock stands as an altar of communion. Isolated from the clatter of the Valley of Trials, it is approached only via the Hidden Path winding up the rocky ridgeline. Aspiring shaman make pilgrimages to this desolate outcrop to drink the traditional sapta, piercing the veil of the physical world to hear the rumblings and whisperings of the earth itself.",["t"]="A Sanctuary of the Elements"}}}}}
t["subzone:splintertree-post"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,296,21.505.0,34.402.0,30.168.0,51.264.0,53.198.0,52.156.0",["h"]="560039",["n"]="Puesto del Hachazo",["s"]="Puesto del Hachazo. El Puesto del Hachazo es la principal fortaleza de la Horda en el este de Vallefresno, situada al noroeste de Cerro Lumbrevil. Establecido por Grommash Grito Infernal y el Clan Grito de Guerra durante la Tercera Guerra, sirve como un baluarte fuertemente fortificado contra los elfos de la noche y como base de operaciones para la expansión territorial. Tallado directamente en los bosques ancestrales, el Puesto del Hachazo sirve como el principal centro militar y logístico de la Horda en el este de Vallefresno. Establecido originalmente por Grommash Grito Infernal y el Clan Grito de Guerra cuando los orcos se adentraron por primera vez en el bosque durante la Tercera Guerra, sigue siendo un enclave fuertemente armado defendido principalmente por exploradores y guerreros orcos y tauren. Dotado de un maestro de vuelo, una posada y líneas de suministro constantes con Orgrimmar, afianza la disputada presencia de la Horda bajo la arboleda.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Splintertree Post is the essential central base camp for adventurers pressing through Ashenvale, offering repairs, respite, and crucial flight routes across Kalimdor.",["race:NightElf"]="To the night elves, this fortress is a bitter scar upon Ashenvale, founded by the very warlord who struck down Cenarius and perpetuated by invaders who butcher their ancient trees."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It was established by Grommash Hellscream and the Warsong clan when the orcs first pushed into Ashenvale during the Third War to gather timber and establish a foothold.",["al"]={"who built splintertree","splintertree founder","grom splintertree"},["q"]="Who founded Splintertree Post?"},{["a"]="The night elves view Splintertree as an illegal, desecrating intrusion on ancestral lands. Hostility lingers from Grommash's brutal campaigns in the Third War, fueled further by ongoing Horde logging and skirmishes against the nearby elven stronghold of Astranaar.",["al"]={"why are elves attacking","splintertree sentinel attacks","night elf raids splintertree"},["q"]="Why do the night elves frequently attack this base?"},{["a"]="Splintertree Post provides an inn, stable master, mailbox, armor repair, and a wind rider flight master with routes connecting to Orgrimmar, the Crossroads, and other Horde outposts across Kalimdor.",["al"]={"splintertree flight path","splintertree services","splintertree inn"},["q"]="What amenities and travel options are available here?"},{["a"]="The settlement is populated primarily by orcs and tauren, functioning as seasoned scouts, sentries, and frontline officers tasked with holding the frontier.",["al"]={"splintertree guards","who lives in splintertree","splintertree races"},["q"]="Who currently makes up the garrison at Splintertree?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","astranaar","felfire hill","grommash hellscream","splintertree post","vhulgra","warsong clan"},["n"]="Splintertree Post",["s"]="Splintertree Post is the primary Horde fortress in eastern Ashenvale, situated northwest of Felfire Hill. Established by Grommash Hellscream and the Warsong clan during the Third War, it serves as a heavily fortified bulwark against the night elves and a staging ground for territorial expansion.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Carved straight out of the ancient woodlands, Splintertree Post serves as the Horde's main military and logistical hub across eastern Ashenvale. Originally established by Grommash Hellscream and the Warsong clan when orcs first pressed into the forest during the Third War, it remains a heavily armed enclave defended primarily by orcish and tauren scouts and warriors. Armed with a flight master, an inn, and steady supply lines to Orgrimmar, it anchors the Horde's contested presence beneath the canopy.",["t"]="A Frontier Stronghold"},{["b"]="Splintertree Post exists in a state of perpetual readiness. The night elves have neither forgotten nor forgiven Grommash's actions during the war, nor do they tolerate ongoing orcish logging and raids against Astranaar. As a result, the settlement faces constant retaliatory strikes and guerilla attacks from the Sentinels hiding in the surrounding timber, testing the garrison's watchmen at all hours.",["t"]="The Constant Threat of Retaliation"}}}}}
t["subzone:splithoof-crag"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,336,18.447.0,21.318.0,28.145.0,32.105.0,30.196.0,54.155.0",["h"]="7afc50",["n"]="Risco Pezuña Quebrada",["s"]="Risco Pezuña Quebrada. Risco Pezuña Quebrada es un asentamiento fortificado de los centauros Galak, resguardado a lo largo de los acantilados septentrionales de Las Mil Agujas. Sirve como uno de los principales enclaves de la tribu junto a las altas mesetas, custodiando la entrada a Campamento Pezuña Quebrada. Los viajeros que cruzan el fondo del cañón deben enfrentarse a las agresivas patrullas Galak que merodean cerca de los riscos. Ubicado contra la escarpada pared rocosa septentrional de Las Mil Agujas, Risco Pezuña Quebrada se encuentra justo al este de la imponente Cumbre de la Nube Negra. Es un asentamiento consolidado de los centauros Galak, provisto de toscos campamentos de tiendas y senderos de tierra que atraviesan los riscos. En el corazón de la aldea, contra la ladera del acantilado, se halla Campamento Pezuña Quebrada, una caverna subterránea que alberga la Pezuña Partida, una antigua reliquia de los centauros protegida por un brasero sagrado.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Controlling the passage beneath the crags is vital for ensuring secure travel between the southern Barrens, Freewind Post, and the Shimmering Flats.",["race:Tauren"]="The long-standing hostility between tauren and centaur makes Splithoof Crag an immediate concern for Horde scouts monitoring hostile activity throughout Thousand Needles."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The settlement belongs to the Galak centaur tribe, one of the prominent clans inhabiting Thousand Needles alongside the hostile Grimtotem tauren.",["al"]={"who is at splithoof crag","splithoof crag mobs","centaur in splithoof crag"},["q"]="Who lives in Splithoof Crag?"},{["a"]="It lies along the northern canyon wall of Thousand Needles, situated directly east of Darkcloud Pinnacle.",["al"]={"where is splithoof crag","splithoof crag location"},["q"]="Where is Splithoof Crag located?"},{["a"]="Splithoof Hold is the central cavern of the village. Deep within its chambers, the Galak guard the Cloven Hoof, an ancient tribal artifact shielded by a sacred flame burning in an ancient brazier.",["al"]={"what is splithoof hold","cave in splithoof crag"},["q"]="What is inside Splithoof Hold?"},{["a"]="No. The Galak centaur and the Grimtotem tauren on Darkcloud Pinnacle are bitter territorial rivals, fighting for dominance over this stretch of the canyon.",["al"]={"grimtotem and galak","centaur and tauren relation"},["q"]="Are the centaur here allied with the nearby Grimtotem?"}},["kw"]={"centaur","cloven hoof","darkcloud pinnacle","galak","splithoof crag","splithoof hold","thousand needles"},["n"]="Splithoof Crag",["s"]="Splithoof Crag is a fortified settlement of the Galak centaur, tucked along the northern cliffs of Thousand Needles. It serves as one of the tribe's major enclaves alongside the high mesas, guarding the entrance to Splithoof Hold. Travelers traversing the canyon floor must contend with aggressive Galak patrols roaming near the bluffs.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Nestled against the sheer northern rock face of Thousand Needles, Splithoof Crag sits just east of the towering Darkcloud Pinnacle. It is an established enclave of the Galak centaur, complete with crude tent encampments and dirt pathways cutting through the crags. At the heart of the village against the cliffside lies Splithoof Hold, a subterranean cavern holding the Cloven Hoof, an ancient relic of the centaur safeguarded by a sacred brazier.",["t"]="A Galak Stronghold"},{["b"]="The Galak fiercely contest this corner of the canyon, clashing with any travelers, Horde expeditions, or tauren scouting parties wandering beneath their bluffs. While the Grimtotem occupy the soaring pinnacles nearby, the centaur hold firm control of this canyon ravine and the caverns burrowed deep beneath the stone.",["t"]="Defending the Caverns"}}}}}
t["subzone:splithoof-hold"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,255,17.285.0,16.278.0,32.203.0,28.156.0,24.174.0",["h"]="ce26d5",["n"]="Campamento Pezuña Quebrada",["s"]="Campamento Pezuña Quebrada. Campamento Pezuña Quebrada es una profunda fortaleza cavernosa excavada en la piedra de Risco Pezuña Quebrada, en Las Mil Agujas. Ocupada por la tribu de centauros Galak, la caverna sirve como guarida fortificada y alberga el Ancient Brazier, un lugar que contiene una llama sagrada que arde eternamente. Oculto en el interior de Risco Pezuña Quebrada, Campamento Pezuña Quebrada sirve como reducto fortificado para los centauros Galak. A diferencia del fondo del cañón azotado por el viento, esta cueva cerrada les ofrece refugio, puntos de estrangulamiento fáciles de defender y un santuario seguro frente a tribus rivales y viajeros que cruzan Las Mil Agujas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Shaman"]="The existence of an eternal flame burning deep within a dark stone cavern draws the attention of any spiritualist attuned to the primal mysteries of elemental fire.",["race:Tauren"]="The Galak centaur remain sworn blood enemies of the tauren, making any stronghold they maintain in Thousand Needles an immediate threat to the peace of Freewind Post."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Splithoof Hold is situated within the crags and ramparts of Splithoof Crag, along the northern cliffs of Thousand Needles. It is entered through a cave opening nestled inside the main centaur settlement.",["al"]={"splithoof hold location","where is splithoof hold","how to find splithoof hold"},["q"]="Where is Splithoof Hold located?"},{["a"]="The cavern is held by the Galak centaur tribe, who aggressively defend the cave against outsiders, beast incursions, and the nearby tauren of Freewind Post.",["al"]={"who lives in splithoof hold","splithoof hold mobs","who owns splithoof hold"},["q"]="Who controls Splithoof Hold?"},{["a"]="Beyond hostile Galak centaur defenders, the cave houses the Ancient Brazier, an artifact that keeps the mystical Sacred Flame burning eternally within the depths of the rock.",["al"]={"what is in splithoof hold","ancient brazier location","sacred flame splithoof"},["q"]="What is inside the hold?"}},["kw"]={"ancient brazier","galak centaur","sacred flame","splithoof crag","splithoof hold","thousand needles"},["n"]="Splithoof Hold",["s"]="Splithoof Hold is a deep cavern stronghold carved into the stone of Splithoof Crag in Thousand Needles. Held by the Galak centaur tribe, the cavern serves as a fortified den and houses the Ancient Brazier, a site holding an eternally burning sacred flame.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away inside Splithoof Crag, Splithoof Hold serves as a fortified redoubt for the Galak centaur. Unlike the windswept canyon floor, this enclosed cave offers them shelter, defensible chokepoints, and a secure sanctuary from rival tribes and travelers passing through the Needles.",["t"]="A Centaur Bastion"},{["b"]="Deep within the shadowed recesses of the hold lies an ancient brazier cradling the Sacred Flame. This mystic fire burns incessantly, serving as a focal point of power and ritual reverence for the centaur and an object of deep curiosity for spiritual wanderers across the canyon.",["t"]="The Sacred Flame"}}}}}
t["subzone:starbreeze-village"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,322,15.444.0,23.426.1,36.225.0,36.174.0,36.104.0,33.169.0",["h"]="3f7da7",["n"]="Aldea Brisa Estelar",["s"]="Aldea Brisa Estelar. La Aldea Brisa Estelar es un asentamiento abandonado de elfos de la noche situado al este de Dolanaar, en Teldrassil. Antaño una tranquila aldea boscosa, recientemente ha caído en manos de los enloquecidos fúrbolgs de la tribu Tuercepinos. El asentamiento en ruinas se alza ahora como un patente símbolo de la creciente corrupción que se filtra por las raíces del Árbol del Mundo. Situada al sureste de Cañada Umbría y justo al final del camino desde Dolanaar, la Aldea Brisa Estelar fue antaño el hogar de pacíficas familias de elfos de la noche que vivían bajo las ramas de Teldrassil. Hoy en día, la aldea se encuentra en ruinas y sus estructuras de madera están invadidas por agresivos fúrbolgs Tuercepinos. Enloquecidos por una siniestra corrupción que aflige las ramas del Árbol del Mundo, estos hombres-bestia expulsaron a los residentes elfos y ahora defienden ferozmente los terrenos en ruinas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="The madness consuming the Gnarlpine furbolgs and the defilement of Starbreeze Village directly challenge the Cenarion Circle's charge to restore balance to Teldrassil's wildlife.",["race:NightElf"]="Seeing an elven settlement so close to Dolanaar fall into ruin is a painful reminder of Teldrassil's precarious state and the corruption gnawing at the World Tree."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The village was overrun when the Gnarlpine furbolgs fell prey to a spreading corruption within Teldrassil. Driven mad and violent, the furbolgs attacked the night elf inhabitants, forcing them to flee and abandon their homes.",["al"]={"what happened to starbreeze","why is starbreeze ruined","starbreeze empty"},["q"]="Why is Starbreeze Village abandoned?"},{["a"]="Hostile Gnarlpine furbolgs now occupy the village. Prominent figures among them include the wandering patrol Uruson and the corrupt figure known as Ferocitas the Dream Eater.",["al"]={"who is in starbreeze","starbreeze mobs","who took over starbreeze"},["q"]="Who lives in Starbreeze Village now?"},{["a"]="Starbreeze Village is located in eastern Teldrassil, lying southeast of Shadowglen and east of Dolanaar.",["al"]={"where is starbreeze","starbreeze map location","how to find starbreeze"},["q"]="Where is Starbreeze Village located?"},{["a"]="Ferocitas is a dangerous, corrupted creature found on the outskirts of Starbreeze Village, associated with the dark forces driving the local Gnarlpine tribe into frenzy.",["al"]={"ferocitas lore","who is ferocitas","ferocitas starbreeze"},["q"]="Who is Ferocitas the Dream Eater?"}},["kw"]={"dolanaar","ferocitas","furbolg","gnarlpine","starbreeze","teldrassil","uruson","village"},["n"]="Starbreeze Village",["s"]="Starbreeze Village is an abandoned night elf settlement situated east of Dolanaar in Teldrassil. Once a tranquil woodland hamlet, it has recently fallen to the maddened furbolgs of the Gnarlpine tribe. The ruined settlement now stands as a glaring symbol of the growing corruption seeping into the roots of the World Tree.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Located southeast of Shadowglen and just down the road from Dolanaar, Starbreeze Village was once home to peaceful night elf families living beneath the boughs of Teldrassil. Today, the village lies in shambles, its wooden structures overrun by aggressive Gnarlpine furbolgs. Driven wild by a sinister corruption afflicting the boughs of the World Tree, the beast-men drove the elven residents out and now defend the ruined grounds ferociously.",["t"]="A Fallen Hamlet"},{["b"]="The Gnarlpine presence in the village is not merely an ordinary territorial raid. Lurking on the outskirts of the settlement is Ferocitas the Dream Eater, an enigmatic, corrupted entity whose presence suggests dark, foul magic is actively driving the furbolgs mad. Together with hulking beasts like Uruson who prowl the paths, these invaders make Starbreeze an active danger to travelers journeying through eastern Teldrassil.",["t"]="The Threat of Ferocitas"}}}}}
t["subzone:steelgrill-s-depot"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,272,28.601.0,27.200.0,19.189.0,33.150.0",["h"]="b0c7b4",["n"]="Almacén de Brasacerada",["s"]="Almacén de Brasacerada. El Almacén de Brasacerada es un bullicioso taller de ingeniería y estación de reparación situado justo al este de Kharanos, en Dun Morogh. Supervisado por Beldin Brasacerada y una cuadrilla de artesanos, sirve como núcleo de primera línea para el mantenimiento de vehículos, transportes de suministros de manitas y labores de rescate de chatarra. Ubicado junto al nevado camino al este de Kharanos, el Almacén de Brasacerada bulle con el estrépito del metal al chocar, el silbido de los respiraderos de vapor y el zumbido de motores experimentales. Mineros enanos y excéntricos ingenieros gnomos se congregan aquí entre maquinaria pesada, armazones andantes mecanizados y reservas de mineral en bruto extraído de las canteras cercanas. Ante los incesantes altercados de los troggs y la escasez de suministros mecánicos que asolan Dun Morogh, Beldin Brasacerada y su cuadrilla mantienen la maquinaria de la Alianza en funcionamiento, convirtiéndose en una parada indispensable para los viajeros que buscan piezas de repuesto o asesoramiento técnico en mitad del frío cortante.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Engineering"]="The depot is an open-air laboratory surrounded by steam machinery and tinkering supplies, making it a natural rest stop for aspiring engineers traveling through Dun Morogh.",["race:Gnome"]="Working closely with their dwarven hosts, exiled gnomish tinkers often use the depot's forge fires and spare components to keep their salvaged contraptions running."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Steelgrill's Depot is an engineering workshop and outpost in Dun Morogh, located just down the road east of Kharanos. It caters to miners, tinkerers, and field technicians maintaining heavy machinery.",["al"]={"steelgrill depot","what is this place","steelgrills"},["q"]="What is Steelgrill's Depot?"},{["a"]="The depot is managed by the Steelgrill family, notably Beldin Steelgrill, alongside fellow dwarven and gnomish crafters who maintain the surrounding machinery and oversee mining operations.",["al"]={"who leads steelgrills","who runs steelgrill depot","belbi steelgrill"},["q"]="Who runs the depot?"},{["a"]="The depot houses trade suppliers, repair services, and trainers for craftsmen looking to hone their engineering and gathering skills out in the field.",["al"]={"trainers at steelgrills","what can i do here","steelgrills depot services"},["q"]="What services are available here?"}},["kw"]={"belbi steelgrill","dun morogh","engineering","kharanos","steelgrill","steelgrill's depot","workshop"},["n"]="Steelgrill's Depot",["s"]="Steelgrill's Depot is a bustling engineering workshop and repair station situated directly east of Kharanos in Dun Morogh. Overseen by Beldin Steelgrill and a crew of craftsmen, it serves as a frontline hub for vehicle maintenance, tinker supply runs, and salvage efforts.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Nestled just off the snowy road east of Kharanos, Steelgrill's Depot buzzes with the clamor of clanking metal, hissing steam vents, and the hum of experimental engines. Dwarven miners and eccentric gnome engineers gather here amid heavy machinery, mechanized walking frames, and stockpiles of raw ores hauled out from nearby quarries. With Dun Morogh facing relentless trogg disruptions and mechanical supply shortages, Beldin Steelgrill and his crew keep Alliance machinery in working order, serving as an indispensable stop for travelers seeking spare parts or technical guidance in the bitter cold.",["t"]="A Bastion of Steam and Steel"}}}}}
t["subzone:stillwater-pond"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,272,16.533.0,20.437.0,48.231.0,42.196.0,46.178.0,33.129.0",["h"]="157ac5",["n"]="Charca Aguaserena",["s"]="Charca Aguaserena. La Charca Aguaserena es una masa de agua tranquila y estancada situada justo al oeste de Rémol, en los Claros de Tirisfal. En su día fue un querido lugar de pícnic y baño para los niños vivos de Lordaeron, pero se ha degradado hasta convertirse en una poza turbia habitada por peces esqueléticos y rondada por peligrosos carroñeros. Antes de la Tercera Guerra y los estragos de la Plaga de la no-muerte, la Charca Aguaserena servía como un tranquilo retiro para las gentes de los Claros de Tirisfal. Las familias de las aldeas cercanas se reunían en sus orillas cubiertas de hierba para hacer pícnics por la tarde, y los niños demasiado pequeños para aventurarse en las traicioneras profundidades del Lago Aguasclaras aprendían a nadar en sus aguas poco profundas. Hoy en día, sus idílicas aguas se han vuelto grises y sin vida. Los vivos desaparecieron hace mucho, dejando solo peces esqueléticos que cruzan bajo la superficie y no-muertos errantes que deambulan por los bosques circundantes.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="The blighted wildlife around the pond, including feral darkhounds like Bayne, makes the area a hazardous hunting ground for scouts patrolling the outskirts of Brill.",["race:Undead"]="For Forsaken who retain memories of life in Lordaeron, Stillwater Pond stands as a grim reminder of lost childhood days spent picnicking and swimming along its once-clear banks."},["faq"]={{["a"]="In the days of human Lordaeron, Stillwater Pond was a scenic and popular spot for local picnics. Because it was shallow and calmer than the expansive Brightwater Lake, families frequently brought young children here to swim safely.",["al"]={"stillwater pond history","what was stillwater pond used for","tirisfal swimming spot"},["q"]="What was Stillwater Pond like before the Plague?"},{["a"]="Normal aquatic life did not survive the blighting of Tirisfal. The only things swimming beneath the gray surface are the animated, skeletal remains of fish left behind by the Scourge's corruption.",["al"]={"stillwater pond fish","what lives in stillwater pond","stillwater creatures"},["q"]="Is there anything living in the water now?"},{["a"]="Apart from mindless undead wandering the glades, the most notorious threat along the shore is Bayne, an unusually powerful and aggressive darkhound who feeds on unwary travelers.",["al"]={"stillwater pond monsters","who is bayne","darkhound near brill"},["q"]="What dangerous creatures wander near the pond?"},{["a"]="Stillwater Pond sits in central Tirisfal Glades, directly west of the town of Brill and southwest of the larger Brightwater Lake.",["al"]={"where is stillwater pond","stillwater pond location","how to find stillwater pond"},["q"]="Where is Stillwater Pond located?"}},["kw"]={"bayne","brightwater lake","brill","darkhound","skeletal fish","stillwater pond","tirisfal glades"},["n"]="Stillwater Pond",["s"]="Stillwater Pond is a quiet, stagnant body of water resting just west of Brill in Tirisfal Glades. Once a beloved picnic and swimming spot for the living children of Lordaeron, it has decayed into a murky pool inhabited by skeletal fish and prowled by dangerous scavengers.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the Third War and the ravages of the Plague of Undeath, Stillwater Pond served as a tranquil retreat for the folk of Tirisfal Glades. Families from nearby hamlets gathered on its grassy banks for afternoon picnics, and children too young to brave the treacherous depths of Brightwater Lake learned to swim in its shallows. Today, the idyllic waters have turned lifeless and gray. The living have long vanished, leaving only skeletal fish darting beneath the surface and wandering undead drifting through the surrounding woods.",["t"]="A Ruined Respite"},{["b"]="Though quiet compared to the besieged roads and contested farms of Tirisfal, Stillwater Pond holds its own perils. The murky waters provide water only to the blighted beasts of the glades, most notably a ferocious darkhound named Bayne who stalks the shoreline. Travelers cutting through the western meadows on their way toward Brill must tread carefully, as predatory beasts and aimless zombies frequently linger along the water's edge.",["t"]="Prowlers in the Mist"}}}}}
t["subzone:stone-cairn-lake"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,325,19.553.0,18.454.0,34.181.0,46.140.0,42.160.0,42.110.0",["h"]="33fffd",["n"]="Lago del Hito",["s"]="Lago del Hito. El Lago del Hito es una masa de agua en forma de anillo situada en el noreste de Bosque de Elwynn. En su centro yace una isla coronada por la Vigilia de los Héroes, un monumento conmemorativo a los caídos en la Primera Guerra. Antaño un lugar tranquilo para la reflexión, el lago se ve ahora perturbado por múrlocs hostiles a lo largo de sus orillas y magos renegados que ocupan la isla. El Lago del Hito debe su nombre al prominente hito de piedra erigido en la gran isla de su centro. Conocido como la Vigilia de los Héroes, este monumento se levantó para honrar las graves pérdidas de vidas humanas sufridas durante la Primera Guerra contra la Horda orca. Antaño, familias y peregrinos viajaban a la isla con total seguridad para presentar sus respetos a los caídos, contemplando a través de las aguas tranquilas la solemne mampostería. Hoy en día, sin embargo, peligrosos magos renegados han establecido un campamento junto al monumento, convirtiendo un lugar sagrado de recuerdo en un reducto hostil.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Mining"]="The bluffs and hills encircling Stone Cairn Lake boast one of the heaviest concentrations of copper deposits in all of Elwynn Forest, making it a lucrative stop for aspiring blacksmiths and engineers.",["race:Human"]="The central island represents a deeply personal memorial for the Kingdom of Stormwind, honoring those lost when the kingdom fell during the First War."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The lake takes its name from Heroes' Vigil, a stone cairn monument raised on the central island to commemorate the Alliance soldiers and civilians who perished during the First War.",["al"]={"stone cairn name","why stone cairn","origin of the name"},["q"]="Why is it called Stone Cairn Lake?"},{["a"]="The island is overrun by rogue wizards and renegades who have chased away ordinary pilgrims and set up a fortified camp around the memorial.",["al"]={"who is on the island","island wizards","rogue mages on lake"},["q"]="Who is currently occupying the central island?"},{["a"]="A local tribe of murlocs has settled the southern shallows and riverbanks, building primitive huts and claiming the plentiful fishing waters as their territory.",["al"]={"murlocs at stone cairn","lake murlocs","south shore huts"},["q"]="Why are murlocs gathered around the water?"},{["a"]="The monument is known as Heroes' Vigil, featuring a stone cairn often referred to as the Stone of Remembrance.",["al"]={"island memorial name","monument name","stone cairn shrine"},["q"]="What is the memorial on the island called?"}},["kw"]={"copper","elwynn forest","first war","heroes' vigil","murloc","rogue wizards","stone cairn lake","stone of remembrance"},["n"]="Stone Cairn Lake",["s"]="Stone Cairn Lake is a ring-shaped body of water resting in northeastern Elwynn Forest. At its center lies an island crowned with Heroes' Vigil, a memorial to the fallen of the First War. Once a tranquil site for reflection, the lake is now troubled by hostile murlocs along its shores and renegade wizards occupying the isle.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Stone Cairn Lake earns its name from the prominent stone memorial erected on the large island in its center. Known as Heroes' Vigil, this monument was raised to honor the heavy loss of human life suffered during the First War against the Orcish Horde. Families and pilgrims once traveled safely to the island to pay respects to the fallen, gazing across the calm waters at the solemn stonework. Today, however, dangerous renegade wizards have established a camp directly beside the memorial, turning a place of sacred remembrance into a hostile redoubt.",["t"]="A Monument Besieged"},{["b"]="Surrounding the ring-shaped lake is a scenic shoreline that has grown increasingly dangerous for locals and travelers. A tribe of aggressive murlocs has claimed the southern banks, erecting crude huts along the waterline and harassing anyone who draws near. Beyond its dangers, the hills and outcrops encircling the lake are rich in mineral veins, making the perimeter a frequent destination for prospectors and miners willing to brave the local threats.",["t"]="Shores of the Lake"}}}}}
t["subzone:stonebull-lake"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,298,19.448.0,32.132.0,44.147.0,46.222.0",["h"]="a87823",["n"]="Lago Toro de Piedra",["s"]="Lago Toro de Piedra. El Lago Toro de Piedra es una serena masa de agua en forma de herradura que rodea el Poblado Pezuña de Sangre, en el centro de Mulgore. Alimentado por las prístinas escorrentías naturales de las llanuras, proporciona agua dulce vital, abundante pesca y costas tranquilas para los jóvenes tauren que alcanzan la edad adulta bajo la guía de Cairne Pezuña de Sangre. Bordeando el Poblado Pezuña de Sangre por tres lados, el Lago Toro de Piedra define la geografía del centro de Mulgore. Un puente de madera cruza el tramo más estrecho del lago, albergando el camino principal de tierra entre el asentamiento y la gran meseta de Cima del Trueno hacia el norte. Sus tranquilas aguas están repletas de peces autóctonos, lo que convierte sus orillas en el lugar predilecto de cazadores que descansan, viajeros agotados y aprendices de pescador que aprenden su oficio bajo el inmenso cielo abierto.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Tauren"]="For the tauren establishing their homes across Mulgore, Stonebull Lake provides gentle sustenance and a reminder of the Earth Mother's bounty near their capital."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Stonebull Lake is located in central Mulgore. It forms a horseshoe around Bloodhoof Village, flanking the settlement on three sides.",["al"]={"stonebull lake location","where is stonebull lake","mulgore lake"},["q"]="Where is Stonebull Lake located?"},{["a"]="The bridge crosses the narrowest part of Stonebull Lake to carry the main road connecting Bloodhoof Village directly to Thunder Bluff in the north.",["al"]={"stonebull bridge","bridge near bloodhoof","road over stonebull lake"},["q"]="What is the bridge across the lake used for?"},{["a"]="The lake is an essential freshwater source and a vital fishing spot for the inhabitants of Bloodhoof Village. It also offers a quiet place of contemplation and gathering for young tauren braves training in central Mulgore.",["al"]={"why does stonebull lake matter","purpose of stonebull lake"},["q"]="Why is Stonebull Lake important to the tauren?"}},["kw"]={"bloodhoof village","fishing","lake","mulgore","stonebull lake","thunder bluff"},["n"]="Stonebull Lake",["s"]="Stonebull Lake is a serene, horseshoe-shaped body of water wrapping around Bloodhoof Village in central Mulgore. Fed by the pristine natural runoff of the plains, it provides vital fresh water, abundant fish, and peaceful shores for the young tauren coming of age under Cairne Bloodhoof's guidance.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Curving around Bloodhoof Village on three sides, Stonebull Lake defines the geography of central Mulgore. A wooden bridge crosses the lake's narrowest stretch, carrying the main dirt road between the settlement and the great mesa of Thunder Bluff to the north. Its calm waters are filled with native fish, making its banks a favored spot for resting hunters, weary travelers, and apprentice fishers learning their trade under the sweeping open sky.",["t"]="Waters of the Plain"}}}}}
t["subzone:stonefield-farm"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,190,18.517.0,58.248.0,29.124.0,38.239.0",["h"]="14d1c9",["n"]="La Granja Pedregosa",["s"]="La Granja Pedregosa. La Granja Pedregosa es una hacienda en activo situada en el sur del Bosque de Elwynn. Es el hogar de la familia Stonefield, que lleva mucho tiempo enzarzada en una amarga disputa con sus vecinos, los Maclure. Enclavada entre las verdes colinas al sur de Villadorada, La Granja Pedregosa produce cosechas para el reino mientras mantiene un rencor feroz y prolongado durante décadas contra Los Viñedos de Maclure cercanos. La mala sangre entre ambos hogares da lugar a disputas mezquinas, acusaciones mutuas de robo y una tensión constante. Sin embargo, bajo estas riñas hostiles, el joven Tommy Joe Pedregosa se ha enamorado en secreto de Maybell Maclure, forjando un discreto romance que podría tender puentes entre las familias o desatar aún más indignación.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Human"]="For humans starting out from Northshire, the squabbles between the Stonefields and Maclures offer a lighthearted look at rural kingdom life beyond the threat of bandits and gnolls."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Stonefield and Maclure families hold a long-standing, stubborn rivalry in southern Elwynn Forest. They constantly accuse one another of trespassing, petty theft, and general wrongdoing, refusing to cooperate on even simple neighborhood matters.",["al"]={"stonefield maclure feud","why are stonefields fighting","stonefield rivals"},["q"]="What is the feud between the Stonefields and the Maclures?"},{["a"]="The farmstead is managed by the Stonefield clan, including Gramma Stonefield, Ma Stonefield, and young Tommy Joe Stonefield.",["al"]={"stonefield npcs","who is at stonefield farm"},["q"]="Who lives at Stonefield Farm?"},{["a"]="Despite the bitter hostility between the two households, Tommy Joe Stonefield is secretly in love with Maybell Maclure. The two lovers rely on sympathetic travelers to pass messages and gifts back and forth without their families noticing.",["al"]={"tommy joe secret","tommy joe romance","stonefield love"},["q"]="What is Tommy Joe Stonefield's secret?"}},["kw"]={"elwynn forest","gramma stonefield","maclure","stonefield","stonefield farm","tommy joe"},["n"]="Stonefield Farm",["s"]="Stonefield Farm is a working homestead situated in southern Elwynn Forest. It is home to the Stonefield family, who have long been locked in a bitter feud with their neighbors, the Maclures.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Nestled in the rolling greenery south of Goldshire, Stonefield Farm produces crops for the realm while maintaining a fierce, decades-long grudge against the nearby Maclure Vineyards. The bad blood between the households leads to petty squabbles, mutual accusations of theft, and constant tension. Yet beneath the hostile bickering, young Tommy Joe Stonefield has fallen secretly in love with Maybell Maclure, creating a quiet romance that could either bridge the divide between the families or ignite further outrage.",["t"]="A Bitter Homestead"}}}}}
t["subzone:stonefire-tavern"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,284,20.513.0,38.120.0,34.97.0,43.122.0,26.136.0",["h"]="83e83c",["n"]="Taberna Fuego de Piedra",["s"]="Taberna Fuego de Piedra. La Taberna Fuego de Piedra es la posada principal que atiende a los viajeros dentro de la ciudad montañosa de Forjaz. Situada en el bullicioso Distrito Comercial, justo al norte de las puertas de la ciudad, ofrece un cálido hogar, fuerte cerveza enana y un lugar de descanso para los aventureros que llegan desde todo Khaz Modan. Ubicada inmediatamente al norte de las puertas de la fortaleza en el Distrito Comercial, la Taberna Fuego de Piedra funciona como la taberna más destacada de Forjaz. Regentada por el Tabernero Brebefuego junto a su hija Gwenna, la posada ofrece a los fatigados caminantes comidas copiosas, cervezas locales y alojamiento bajo la montaña. Ya sea buscando respiro de las duras nieves montañosas de Dun Morogh o con la intención de intercambiar relatos y provisiones antes de adentrarse en las profundidades de la ciudad, los viajeros de todos los rincones de la Alianza se reúnen con frecuencia alrededor de su crepitante fuego.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="As the closest major inn to the Ironforge front gates, the Stonefire is often the central staging ground for Alliance travelers visiting the dwarven capital.",["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves returning from expeditions across Khaz Modan, the Stonefire Tavern is the first place in the capital to grab a cold pint of Firebrew ale and catch up on local gossip."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The tavern sits in the Commons district of Ironforge, just a short walk north after passing through the main city gates.",["al"]={"stonefire tavern location","ironforge inn location","where is stonefire"},["q"]="Where is the Stonefire Tavern located?"},{["a"]="The tavern is managed by Innkeeper Firebrew with the assistance of his daughter, Gwenna Firebrew.",["al"]={"who runs stonefire tavern","stonefire innkeeper","firebrew inn"},["q"]="Who operates the Stonefire Tavern?"},{["a"]="Yes. Innkeeper Firebrew welcomes Alliance travelers seeking to make the Stonefire Tavern their home base within Ironforge.",["al"]={"set hearth ironforge","ironforge home inn","hearthstone stonefire"},["q"]="Can travelers bind their hearthstones here?"},{["a"]="Right outside the tavern entrance sits a city mailbox, and the surrounding Commons are filled with banks, merchants, and trade supplies.",["al"]={"stonefire services","mailbox near stonefire"},["q"]="What amenities are nearby?"}},["kw"]={"commons","dwarven inn","gwenna firebrew","innkeeper firebrew","ironforge","khaz modan","stonefire tavern"},["n"]="Stonefire Tavern",["s"]="The Stonefire Tavern is the primary inn serving travelers inside the mountain city of Ironforge. Situated in the bustling Commons district just north of the city gates, it provides a warm hearth, strong dwarven ale, and a resting place for adventurers arriving from across Khaz Modan.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Located immediately north of the fortress gates in the Commons, the Stonefire Tavern serves as the premier public house in Ironforge. Run by Innkeeper Firebrew alongside his daughter Gwenna, the inn offers weary wayfarers hearty meals, local brews, and lodging beneath the mountain. Whether seeking respite from the harsh mountain snows of Dun Morogh or looking to trade tales and supplies before venturing deep into the city, travelers from all corners of the Alliance routinely gather around its roaring hearth.",["t"]="Heart of the Commons"}}}}}
t["subzone:stonetalon-peak"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,269,22.491.0,21.593.0,70.293.0,40.291.0,39.233.0,36.239.0",["h"]="a4d216",["n"]="Cima del Espolón",["s"]="Cima del Espolón. La Cima del Espolón es un antiguo santuario de los elfos de la noche resguardado en un frondoso valle alpino en el extremo noroccidental de Sierra Espolón. Sagrado para los kaldorei y cuidado por druidas locales, sirve como el principal bastión de la Alianza en estas escarpadas alturas. Encaramada muy por encima del polvo árido de las cordilleras inferiores, la Cima del Espolón se abre a un santuario exuberante y envuelto en brumas. Considerado sagrado durante mucho tiempo e impregnado de magia ancestral, el valle alberga ruinas que datan de milenios atrás, cuando la región albergaba templos en honor a la reina Azshara antes del Gran Cataclismo. En la era moderna, las centinelas y los druidas kaldorei han restablecido aquí una pacífica custodia, manteniendo un refugio tranquilo dotado de un túmulo y un nido de vuelo vital para la Alianza.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="The sanctuary is deeply intertwined with Cenarion history and the sacred Talon Den, making it an essential place of pilgrimage and defense for wardens of the wild.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stonetalon Peak is your sole fortified foothold in the western mountains, offering vital respite, flight paths, and questing aid amidst hostile territory."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Stonetalon Peak rests within a sheltered high-altitude basin suffused with ancient magic. The dedicated care of the night elves and the druids of the nearby Talon Den has preserved a vibrant, forested sanctuary where vegetation flourishes in sharp contrast to the charred, jagged cliffs below.",["al"]={"why is stonetalon peak green","why forest in stonetalon peak","stonetalon peak weather"},["q"]="Why is Stonetalon Peak so green compared to the rest of the mountains?"},{["a"]="Led by the Prophet Medivh's prophetic warnings, both Jaina Proudmoore and Thrall traveled to Stonetalon Peak in search of the Oracle within the mountain's caverns. Their meeting deep inside the stone led them to forge a historic truce, uniting humans and orcs to confront the Burning Legion.",["al"]={"what happened at stonetalon peak warcraft 3","jaina and thrall stonetalon","the oracle stonetalon"},["q"]="What happened here during the Third War?"},{["a"]="The peak is an Alliance outpost, protected and maintained by night elf Sentinels and druids. It serves as the primary safe haven, quest hub, and flight master connection for Alliance adventurers operating in the Stonetalon Mountains.",["al"]={"is stonetalon peak alliance or horde","who lives at stonetalon peak","stonetalon peak faction"},["q"]="Who controls Stonetalon Peak right now?"},{["a"]="The crumbling pillars and marble structures scattered through the vale are remnants of the ancient night elven empire, having once served as temple grounds dedicated to Queen Azshara before her descent into madness and the Great Sundering.",["al"]={"stonetalon peak ruins","old temple stonetalon","azshara temple stonetalon peak"},["q"]="What ancient ruins are located here?"}},["kw"]={"jaina","kaldorei","night elf","oracle","sentinels","stonetalon","stonetalon peak","talon den","thrall"},["n"]="Stonetalon Peak",["s"]="Stonetalon Peak is an ancient night elven sanctuary tucked into a verdant alpine valley at the northwestern edge of the Stonetalon Mountains. Sacred to the kaldorei and cared for by local druids, it serves as the primary bastion of the Alliance in these craggy heights.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched high above the arid dust of the lower ranges, Stonetalon Peak opens into a lush, mist-shrouded sanctuary. Long considered sacred and steeped in ancient magic, the valley holds ruins dating back millennia to when the region housed temples honoring Queen Azshara before the Great Sundering. In the modern era, kaldorei Sentinels and druids have restored a measure of peaceful stewardship here, maintaining a tranquil refuge complete with a barrow den and a vital Alliance flight roost.",["t"]="A Sacred Mountain Vale"},{["b"]="Beyond its idyllic forests and ancient ruins, Stonetalon Peak holds historic weight from the Third War. Guided by the visions of Medivh, both Jaina Proudmoore's human expedition and Thrall's Horde scaled these perilous heights in search of the elusive Oracle dwelling within the mountain's deep caverns. That fateful encounter forced mortal enemies to set aside their blades, laying the foundation for the uneasy pact that stood against the Burning Legion at Mount Hyjal. Today, the peak remains firmly under Sentinel watch, though Horde incursions in the lowlands keep the defenders vigilant.",["t"]="Crossroads of Destiny"}}}}}
t["subzone:stonewatch"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="10,295,17.689.0,23.484.0,34.240.0,35.228.0,52.247.0,69.264.0",["h"]="7d06ce",["n"]="Petravista",["s"]="Petravista. Petravista es un bastión fortificado en el centro de las Montañas Crestagrana, construido para defender las tierras humanas circundantes de las invasiones del norte. Antaño defendida por soldados de Ventormenta, la fortaleza ha caído bajo el brutal control de los orcos Roca Negra, lo que representa una amenaza inmediata para la cercana Villa del Lago. Ubicada sobre los acantilados cerca de las Cascadas Petravista, Petravista consta de una torre y un torreón fuertemente construidos, diseñados para vigilar los accesos desde Las Estepas Ardientes. En su origen en manos de los defensores de Villa del Lago, la fortificación cayó cuando el brujo renegado Morganth forjó una alianza con el clan Roca Negra. Imbuidos de magia oscura, los orcos invasores arrollaron a la guarnición humana local (el 12.º Regimiento de Sables) y se apoderaron de la fortaleza. Aunque Morganth acabó traicionando a sus aliados y se retiró a la cercana Torre de Ilgalar con un ejército de gnolls Pellejo Sombrío, los orcos Roca Negra mantuvieron el control férreo sobre el torreón bajo el mando del general Gath'Ilzogg y el teniente Tharil'zun.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Stonewatch represents one of the most perilous forward incursions of hostile orcs into core Alliance territory, making its recovery vital to the safety of Redridge.",["race:Human"]="The slaughter of the 12th Sabre Regiment and the fall of the keep stand as painful reminders of Lakeshire's vulnerability and Stormwind's political neglect."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Stonewatch is occupied by the Blackrock clan of orcs, under the command of General Gath'Ilzogg and his lieutenant, Tharil'zun. They drove out the kingdom's garrison and now use the stronghold as a staging ground for attacks across Redridge.",["al"]={"who is in stonewatch","who holds stonewatch","stonewatch enemies"},["q"]="Who controls Stonewatch right now?"},{["a"]="The keep fell during a concerted invasion by the Blackrock clan, empowered by the dark sorcery of the rogue human warlock Morganth. Together, they crushed the defenders of the 12th Sabre Regiment and captured the entire complex.",["al"]={"fall of stonewatch","how did stonewatch fall","stonewatch backstory"},["q"]="How did the humans lose Stonewatch?"},{["a"]="Stormwind has refused to allocate sufficient troops to the border regions, leaving Magistrate Solomon and Marshal Marris to defend Redridge alone. Lakeshire relies on visiting adventurers and mercenaries to mount counterattacks against Stonewatch.",["al"]={"why no stormwind help","lakeshire reinforcements"},["q"]="Why isn't Stormwind sending an army to take it back?"},{["a"]="Morganth originally aided the Blackrock orcs in taking Stonewatch, but shortly after their victory, he betrayed his allies. He constructed the nearby Tower of Ilgalar to amass his own retinue of magical thralls and Shadowhide gnolls, attacking orc and human alike.",["al"]={"tower of ilgalar connection","morganth stonewatch"},["q"]="What is the relationship between Stonewatch and the Tower of Ilgalar?"}},["kw"]={"blackrock orcs","gath'ilzogg","lakeshire","morganth","redridge","stonewatch","stonewatch keep","tharil'zun"},["n"]="Stonewatch",["s"]="Stonewatch is a fortified stronghold in central Redridge Mountains, built to defend the surrounding human lands from northern invasions. Formerly manned by Stormwind soldiers, the fortress has fallen under the brutal control of the Blackrock orcs, posing an immediate threat to nearby Lakeshire.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Positioned over the cliffs near Stonewatch Falls, Stonewatch comprises a heavily built tower and keep designed to guard the approaches from the Burning Steppes. Originally held by Lakeshire's defenders, the fortification fell when the rogue warlock Morganth forged an alliance with the Blackrock clan. Infused with dark magic, the invading orcs overwhelmed the local human garrison—the 12th Sabre Regiment—and claimed the fortress. Although Morganth eventually turned on his allies and withdrew to the nearby Tower of Ilgalar with an army of Shadowhide gnolls, the Blackrock orcs retained a stranglehold over the keep under the command of General Gath'Ilzogg and Lieutenant Tharil'zun.",["t"]="A Bastion Overrun"},{["b"]="With Stonewatch firmly garrisoned by hostile orcs, Lakeshire sits directly in the crosshairs of an impending conquest. Cut off from substantial military reinforcements by an indifferent or paralyzed Stormwind House of Nobles, Magistrate Solomon and Marshal Marris have been forced to hire mercenary aid and volunteers. Decapitating the fortress's leadership—targeting both Tharil'zun and Gath'Ilzogg—remains the town's desperate primary hope for relieving the siege on the region.",["t"]="The Threat to Lakeshire"}}}}}
t["subzone:stonewatch-falls"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,292,25.441.0,53.165.0,44.178.0,49.190.0",["h"]="a70a8d",["n"]="Cascadas Petravista",["s"]="Cascadas Petravista. Cascadas Petravista es una pintoresca cascada y una profunda poza de montaña situada en los confines orientales de las Montañas Crestagrana, alimentada por el desagüe del Lago Sempiterno. Cayendo en cascada por la ladera bajo las imponentes alturas de Petravista, sus aguas aisladas están ocupadas por una tribu hostil de múrlocs. Brotando del río oriental del Lago Sempiterno, Cascadas Petravista se precipita por el escarpado terreno situado bajo el bastión de los orcos Roca Negra de Petravista. El agua que se despeña horada una profunda poza resguardada contra la ladera de la montaña. A pesar de su belleza natural, los viajeros rara vez se demoran a admirar la vista; una despiadada banda de múrlocs infesta la poza, construyendo toscas chozas de juncos y atacando a cualquiera que sea lo bastante insensato como para adentrarse en la orilla del agua.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The murloc settlement at Stonewatch Falls represents yet another dangerous pocket of monsters harassing travelers in the already beleaguered eastern Redridge countryside."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The falls are fed by the river draining out of the eastern side of Lake Everstill, tumbling downhill into a secluded mountain basin beneath the cliffs of Stonewatch.",["al"]={"where does stonewatch falls start","falls water source","stonewatch river source"},["q"]="Where does the water from Stonewatch Falls come from?"},{["a"]="A local tribe of murlocs occupies the shores of the falls. They subsist on fish drawn from the deep mountain pool and build rough lean-tos and shoreline shelters along the banks.",["al"]={"what is at stonewatch falls","murlocs at stonewatch falls","mobs near falls"},["q"]="What creatures live around Stonewatch Falls?"},{["a"]="The falls sit at the foot of the hillside directly below Stonewatch and its ruined keep. While Blackrock orcs command the fortified heights above, the murlocs dominate the water basin below.",["al"]={"falls connection to keep","is stonewatch keep near the falls","stonewatch relationship"},["q"]="Is Stonewatch Falls connected to Stonewatch Keep?"}},["kw"]={"lake everstill","murlocs","redridge","stonewatch","stonewatch falls","waterfall"},["n"]="Stonewatch Falls",["s"]="Stonewatch Falls is a scenic waterfall and deep mountain pool situated in the eastern reaches of the Redridge Mountains, fed by the outflow of Lake Everstill. Cascading down the hillside beneath the looming heights of Stonewatch, its isolated waters are claimed by a hostile tribe of murlocs.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Pouring from the eastern river of Lake Everstill, Stonewatch Falls cascades down the rugged terrain beneath the Blackrock orc stronghold of Stonewatch. The plunging water carves out a deep pool tucked against the mountainside. Despite its natural beauty, travelers rarely linger to admire the view; a vicious band of murlocs infests the pool, building crude reed hovels and preying upon any foolish enough to trespass along the water's edge.",["t"]="A Perilous Mountain Basin"}}}}}
t["subzone:stonewatch-keep"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,277,16.665.0,18.585.0,35.214.0,44.202.0,54.219.0,47.240.0",["h"]="1c4e24",["n"]="Fuerte de Petravista",["s"]="Fuerte de Petravista. El Fuerte de Petravista es una fortaleza de piedra que se alza en el este de las Montañas Crestagrana, antaño construida y defendida por el Reino de Ventormenta. Ha caído en manos de una hueste invasora de orcos Rocanegra y sirve como base de operaciones avanzada desde la que sus señores de la guerra aterrorizan Villa del Lago. En sus orígenes, el Fuerte de Petravista defendía las crestas orientales y protegía a los colonos de Villa del Lago contra incursiones hostiles. Esa paz se truncó cuando el brujo renegado Morganth forjó una alianza con el clan Rocanegra. Fortalecidos por la magia oscura, los orcos asaltaron la fortaleza con una ferocidad despiadada, arrollando a los defensores humanos y adueñándose del fuerte. Aunque Morganth abandonó más tarde a sus aliados para erigir la cercana Torre de Ilgalar y subyugar a los gnolls locales, los invasores Rocanegra consolidaron con éxito su dominio sobre Petravista, transformando un antiguo bastión de la Alianza en un punto de partida fortificado para su asalto al valle.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Stonewatch Keep is a painful reminder of Stormwind's strained borders; clearing its ramparts is essential to protecting Lakeshire's vulnerable townsfolk.",["race:Human"]="Human defenders shed blood defending these walls, and liberating the keep helps avenge the fallen soldiers and captives taken by the Blackrock clan."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The keep is currently occupied by the Blackrock clan, led on-site by Warlord Gath'Ilzogg and his lieutenant Tharil'zun. It was formerly an Alliance stronghold defending the town of Lakeshire before it was captured.",["al"]={"who controls stonewatch keep","who lives in stonewatch keep","stonewatch keep enemies"},["q"]="Who owns Stonewatch Keep right now?"},{["a"]="The Blackrock clan allied with the rogue human warlock Morganth. Empowered by Morganth's dark sorcery, the orcs launched a ferocious assault that overwhelmed the human defenders stationed at Stonewatch.",["al"]={"how did orcs get stonewatch","fall of stonewatch keep","why did stonewatch fall"},["q"]="How did the Blackrock orcs capture the keep?"},{["a"]="The Stormwind Army has left Redridge largely neglected due to internal politics and troop shortages across the kingdom. As a result, Lakeshire's town leaders must rely on independent adventurers to deal with the threat.",["al"]={"why no stormwind army","where are the guards","lakeshire army help"},["q"]="Why doesn't the Stormwind Army retake Stonewatch Keep?"},{["a"]="Morganth helped the Blackrock clan conquer Stonewatch Keep, but betrayed them shortly after their victory. He relocated to construct his own lair, the Tower of Ilgalar, using ensorcelled Shadowhide gnolls rather than orcs to do his bidding.",["al"]={"morganth stonewatch","is morganth inside stonewatch keep"},["q"]="What is Morganth's connection to this fortress?"}},["kw"]={"blackrock clan","gath'ilzogg","keeshan","lakeshire","morganth","redridge mountains","stonewatch keep","tharil'zun"},["n"]="Stonewatch Keep",["s"]="Stonewatch Keep is a fortified stone stronghold looming in eastern Redridge Mountains, once built and manned by the Kingdom of Stormwind. It has fallen to an invading host of Blackrock orcs, serving as the forward operational base from which their warlords terrorize Lakeshire.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Stonewatch Keep originally defended the eastern ridges and guarded the settlers of Lakeshire against hostile incursions. That peace shattered when the renegade warlock Morganth struck an alliance with the Blackrock clan. Bolstered by dark magic, the orcs stormed the fortress with vicious ferocity, overwhelming the human defenders and taking the keep for themselves. Although Morganth later abandoned his allies to raise the nearby Tower of Ilgalar and subjugate local gnolls, the Blackrock invaders successfully consolidated their grip over Stonewatch, transforming a former bastion of the Alliance into a fortified staging ground for their assault on the valley.",["t"]="A Fallen Bastion"},{["b"]="Now occupied by a heavy garrison of Blackrock warriors, the keep is overseen by the formidable orcish warlord Gath'Ilzogg and his brutal lieutenant, Tharil'zun. From the stone ramparts, these commanders coordinate raids across Redridge, taking prisoners such as Stormwind's Corporal Keeshan. With the kingdom's military spread thin and unable to dispatch a full regiment to liberate the fortress, Magistrate Solomon and Marshal Marris have been forced to hire mercenary champions to infiltrate the stronghold and execute the Blackrock leadership before Lakeshire is completely overrun.",["t"]="The Warlord's Seat"}}}}}
t["subzone:stonewatch-tower"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,281,18.624.0,25.214.0,40.149.0,49.151.0,32.168.0",["h"]="08a70d",["n"]="Torre de Petravista",["s"]="Torre de Petravista. La Torre de Petravista es una torre de vigilancia de piedra situada dentro de la fortaleza invadida de Petravista, en el noreste de Crestagrana. Antaño mantenida por los defensores de Villa del Lago, el puesto de avanzada fue capturado por el clan Roca Negra para vigilar los riscos circundantes y asegurar su bastión montañoso. Construida por el Reino de Ventormenta para vigilar los pasos de alta montaña sobre el Lago Sempiterno, la Torre de Petravista servía como el puesto de exploración avanzado hermano del Fuerte de Petravista. Desde su elevada posición estratégica, los centinelas podían vigilar fácilmente los riscos orientales y alertar a Villa del Lago de cualquier amenaza que avanzara desde Las Estepas Ardientes. Esa red de alerta temprana se derrumbó cuando los orcos Roca Negra del general Gath'Ilzogg descendieron desde las alturas, arrollando a los defensores humanos y reclamando la fortaleza para su propio esfuerzo bélico. Hoy en día, la torre está repleta de centinelas Roca Negra, lo que garantiza que ningún explorador de la Alianza se acerque a la fortaleza sin ser detectado.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Stonewatch Tower is a grim reminder of how far the Blackrock clan has pushed into Stormwind territory while the kingdom's central army remains absent.",["race:Human"]="For the folk of Lakeshire, seeing orcish standards flying above Stonewatch's towers is an ongoing threat to their very survival."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It is a fortified human watchtower located inside the greater Stonewatch complex in northeastern Redridge Mountains. Originally built to protect the region, it is currently held by invaders from the Blackrock clan.",["al"]={"stonewatch tower lore","what is this tower","stonewatch lookout"},["q"]="What is Stonewatch Tower?"},{["a"]="The tower is occupied by orcs of the Blackrock clan serving under General Gath'Ilzogg, who captured the stronghold from the local humans of Redridge.",["al"]={"who owns stonewatch tower","who is in stonewatch tower","stonewatch tower enemies"},["q"]="Who controls Stonewatch Tower right now?"},{["a"]="Its high elevation allows the Blackrock clan to spot approaching Alliance forces and safeguard the approach to their primary fortress, Stonewatch Keep.",["al"]={"why do orcs want stonewatch tower","strategic importance of stonewatch tower"},["q"]="Why is the tower important to the Blackrock orcs?"},{["a"]="Lakeshire lacks the military manpower to retake Stonewatch on its own and relies on wandering adventurers to thin out the Blackrock garrison holding the tower and keep.",["al"]={"will lakeshire take it back","lakeshire plans for stonewatch tower"},["q"]="Can Lakeshire reclaim the tower?"}},["kw"]={"blackrock clan","gath'ilzogg","lakeshire","redridge","scout tower","stonewatch","stonewatch tower"},["n"]="Stonewatch Tower",["s"]="Stonewatch Tower is a stone guard tower standing within the overrun stronghold of Stonewatch in northeastern Redridge. Once maintained by the defenders of Lakeshire, the outpost was captured by the Blackrock clan to monitor the surrounding ridges and secure their mountain bastion.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Built by the Kingdom of Stormwind to guard the high mountain passes above Lake Everstill, Stonewatch Tower served as the forward scouting sibling to Stonewatch Keep. From its elevated vantage point, sentries could easily watch the eastern ridges and alert Lakeshire to any threats advancing from the Burning Steppes. That early warning network collapsed when General Gath'Ilzogg's Blackrock orcs swept down from the heights, overrunning the human defenders and claiming the stronghold for their own war effort. Today, the tower bristles with Blackrock sentinels, ensuring no Alliance scouts approach the fortress undetected.",["t"]="A Fallen Watchpost"}}}}}
t["subzone:stonewrought-dam"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,239,25.518.0,20.490.0,31.218.0,31.209.0,39.225.0,48.162.0",["h"]="eab96e",["n"]="Presa de las Tres Cabezas",["s"]="Presa de las Tres Cabezas. La Presa de las Tres Cabezas es una colosal maravilla de la ingeniería enana erigida a lo largo del extremo norte de Loch Modan. Retiene las aguas de Loch Modan, creando el enorme lago de las tierras altas mientras drena los Humedales que se encuentran debajo para convertirlos en marismas habitables. Extendiéndose a lo largo del cañón al este de Dun Algaz, la Presa de las Tres Cabezas está considerada una de las mayores hazañas estructurales de la civilización enana. Diseñada por el maestro arquitecto Hierro Negro Franclorn Forgewright, la barrera fue construida utilizando su innovadora técnica de cantería forjada en piedra. Al atrapar las aguas de la cuenca montañosa, la presa duplicó la superficie de Loch Modan a la vez que reducía de forma constante los niveles de agua hacia el norte, permitiendo que la cuenca pantanosa de los Humedales emergiera de un valle que antaño estaba completamente anegado.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Engineering"]="For engineers of any stripe, the dam is a masterclass in hydraulic control and stonewrought load-bearing mechanics, rivaling even the great works beneath Ironforge.",["race:Dwarf"]="The dam stands as a monument to ancient dwarven masonry and architectural ingenuity, though its Dark Iron heritage remains a sore and contested point among Ironforge's historians."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It was designed and overseen by the famous Dark Iron architect Franclorn Forgewright, who invented the stonewrought construction technique. Although built by a Dark Iron master, it serves the Bronzebeard kingdom today.",["al"]={"who made stonewrought dam","creator of the dam","dam architect"},["q"]="Who built the Stonewrought Dam?"},{["a"]="A collapse would be catastrophic. The Loch would rapidly drain and leave Loch Modan an empty crater of mud, while the displaced water would sweep down into the Wetlands as an uncontrollable, devastating flood.",["al"]={"if dam breaks","what if the dam breaks","dam destroyed"},["q"]="What happens if the dam breaks?"},{["a"]="The Dark Iron clan seeks to strike at Ironforge's vital infrastructure and destabilize the region. Crippling the dam would cripple supply lines, drown the northern wetlands, and strike a bitter blow against Bronzebeard pride.",["al"]={"why attack dam","dark iron dam attack"},["q"]="Why are Dark Iron dwarves attacking it?"},{["a"]="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII manages the day-to-day operations and defensive fortifications of the dam, coordinating with Ironforge forces to weed out saboteurs.",["al"]={"who runs the dam","dam engineer"},["q"]="Who is currently in charge of the dam's defense?"}},["kw"]={"dark iron","franclorn forgewright","hinderweir","loch modan","stonewrought dam","the loch","wetlands"},["n"]="Stonewrought Dam",["s"]="The Stonewrought Dam is a colossal dwarven engineering marvel standing along the northern rim of Loch Modan. It holds back the waters of the Loch, creating the massive highland lake while draining the Wetlands below into habitable marshes.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Stretching across the canyon east of Dun Algaz, the Stonewrought Dam is widely regarded as one of the great structural triumphs of dwarven civilization. Designed by the master Dark Iron architect Franclorn Forgewright, the barrier was built using his pioneering stonewrought technique. By trapping the waters of the mountain basin, the dam doubled the surface area of the Loch while steadily lowering water levels to the north, allowing the marshy basin of the Wetlands to emerge from a once completely flooded valley.",["t"]="A Wonder of Dwarven Craft"},{["b"]="Though built under the guidance of a Dark Iron architect, the dam today serves Ironforge—and has become a prime target for Dark Iron saboteurs operating out of the southern mountains. Recent assaults and infiltration attempts have forced Ironforge to station a garrison here under Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII. Guards and engineers patrol the masonry day and night, knowing that any breach would catastrophically drain the Loch and unleash a devastating deluge across the Wetlands below.",["t"]="Sabotage and Defense"}}}}}
t["subzone:stormwind-gate"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,246,28.536.0,35.176.0,56.267.0,21.226.0,42.193.0",["h"]="3a87b7",["n"]="Ventormenta Gate",["s"]="Ventormenta Gate. La Ventormenta Gate es la monumental entrada fortificada que conecta el Bosque de Elwynn con Ciudad de Ventormenta. Custodiado constantemente por centinelas reales, este umbral se alza como el límite principal entre los tranquilos bosques y el majestuoso Valle de los Héroes. Erigiéndose sobre el camino meridional del Bosque de Elwynn, la Ventormenta Gate sirve tanto de baluarte defensivo como de umbral ceremonial para la capital. Los centinelas de la guardia de la Ciudad de Ventormenta mantienen una vigilancia constante a lo largo del portal de piedra, custodiando los accesos desde el bosque mientras patrullas regulares marchan entre el arco exterior y el Valle de los Héroes. A pesar de la persistente agitación en todo Elwynn, los enormes portones de hierro y piedra permanecen abiertos de par en par para dar la bienvenida a viajeros, mercaderes y defensores que regresan al corazón de la Alianza.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The gate represents the safety and endurance of the Grand Alliance, serving as the first glimpse of majesty for traveling soldiers and young adventurers.",["race:Human"]="To the people of Stormwind, returning through these stone arches means returning home to safety after long journeys through Elwynn and beyond."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Passing through the gate from Elwynn Forest brings you directly into the Valley of Heroes, the grand entryway to Stormwind City lined with towering monuments of the Second War.",["al"]={"where does stormwind gate go","what is past the gate","stormwind entrance"},["q"]="Where does the Stormwind Gate lead?"},{["a"]="Stormwind thrives on open trade and steady travel from Goldshire and across the Alliance. While banditry and Defias activity trouble the surrounding woods, the city keeps the passage manned with vigilant guards rather than shutting out its own citizenry and commerce.",["al"]={"why are the gates open","is stormwind gate closed","why open"},["q"]="Why is the gate left open if Elwynn Forest is dangerous?"},{["a"]="The entryway is garrisoned by the Stormwind City Guard. Two sentries stand watch immediately outside in Elwynn Forest, two more guard the inner passage, and armed footmen patrol the bridge leading through the Valley of Heroes.",["al"]={"stormwind gate guards","who defends the gate"},["q"]="Who guards the gates?"},{["a"]="Yes. The open ground around the Stormwind Gate frequently hosts major citywide holidays and seasonal gatherings for the Alliance, serving as an open assembly area outside the crowded districts.",["al"]={"holidays at stormwind gate","events at gate"},["q"]="Are there special events held at the gate?"}},["kw"]={"elwynn forest","goldshire","stormwind city guard","stormwind gate","valley of heroes"},["n"]="Stormwind Gate",["s"]="The Stormwind Gate is the monumental fortified entryway connecting Elwynn Forest to Stormwind City. Guarded constantly by royal sentries, this threshold stands as the primary boundary between the tranquil woodlands and the grand Valley of Heroes.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Towering over the southern road of Elwynn Forest, the Stormwind Gate serves as both a defensive bulwark and a ceremonial threshold for the capital. Sentinels of the Stormwind City Guard maintain a constant watch across the stone portal, guarding the approaches from the forest while regular patrols march between the outer arch and the Valley of Heroes. Despite lingering unrest throughout Elwynn, the massive iron-and-stone gates remain wide open to welcome travelers, merchants, and returning defenders into the heart of the Alliance.",["t"]="The Threshold of the Kingdom"}}}}}
t["subzone:stormwind-keep"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,269,19.466.0,15.482.1,38.178.0,35.249.0,40.232.0,48.194.0",["h"]="b9ab14",["n"]="Castillo de Ventormenta",["s"]="Castillo de Ventormenta. Castillo de Ventormenta se alza sobre la capital como la fortaleza de piedra y sede del poder del Reino de Ventormenta. Reconstruido tras quedar en ruinas en la Primera Guerra, actualmente alberga la corte real del joven rey niño Anduin Wrynn y de su regente, el Alto Señor Bolvar Fordragón. Encaramado sobre una meseta que domina toda la ciudad, Castillo de Ventormenta sirve tanto de palacio como de bastión militar. La fortaleza original fue reducida a cenizas por la Antigua Horda cuando el rey Llane fue asesinado cerca del final de la Primera Guerra. Erigido de nuevo sobre los antiguos cimientos tras recuperar la Alianza el reino, el torreón reconstruido alberga no solo la gran sala del trono y la Sala de Guerra, sino también tranquilos patios ajardinados y la amplia Biblioteca Real.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The keep is the heart of the Alliance's eastern military command, where Bolvar Fordragon and the marshals direct defenses against rising threats across Elwynn, Westfall, and beyond.",["race:Human"]="Rebuilt from ashes after the devastation of the First War, the fortress stands as a testament to the resilience and pride of Stormwind's people."},["faq"]={{["a"]="King Anduin Wrynn technically holds the throne, but because he is only ten years old, Highlord Bolvar Fordragon governs as regent alongside Lady Katrana Prestor as royal advisor.",["al"]={"who is in charge","who leads stormwind","who is the king"},["q"]="Who rules in Stormwind Keep right now?"},{["a"]="King Varian vanished under mysterious circumstances while traveling across the sea to a peace conference in Theramore. His sudden disappearance left the throne vacant, forcing Bolvar and the court to crown young Anduin to ensure political stability.",["al"]={"where is varian","varian missing","what happened to the king"},["q"]="What happened to King Varian Wrynn?"},{["a"]="Yes. Following the murder of King Llane Wrynn by Garona, the Old Horde overwhelmed the city and completely razed the keep. The current fortress was rebuilt upon the ancient foundations after the Alliance prevailed in the Second War.",["al"]={"did the orcs destroy the keep","first war castle destruction"},["q"]="Was the keep destroyed in the First War?"},{["a"]="The complex contains the main throne room, the War Room directly behind it, the Petitioner's Chamber for visiting supplicants, an open garden courtyard, the Royal Gallery, and the Royal Library.",["al"]={"keep rooms","what is inside the keep","wings of stormwind keep"},["q"]="What major wings can be visited inside the keep?"}},["kw"]={"anduin wrynn","bolvar fordragon","castle stormwind","katrana prestor","royal library","stormwind keep","throne room","war room"},["n"]="Stormwind Keep",["s"]="Stormwind Keep stands high above the capital as the stone fortress and seat of power for the Kingdom of Stormwind. Rebuilt after its ruin in the First War, it currently houses the royal court of the young boy-king Anduin Wrynn and his regent, Highlord Bolvar Fordragon.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched upon a plateau overlooking the entire city, Stormwind Keep serves as both a palace and a military bastion. The original stronghold was burned to the ground by the Old Horde when King Llane was assassinated near the end of the First War. Raised anew upon the old foundations after the Alliance reclaimed the kingdom, the reconstructed keep houses not only the grand throne room and the War Room, but peaceful garden courtyards and the expansive Royal Library.",["t"]="The Rebuilt Citadel"},{["b"]="Behind the keep's banners and polished stone lies an uneasy peace. With King Varian Wrynn mysteriously missing en route to a diplomatic summit at Theramore, governance rests on ten-year-old King Anduin Wrynn. Effective rule falls to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon and the noble Lady Katrana Prestor. While Bolvar handles defense and military affairs, court politics remain paralyzed by aristocratic infighting, leaving the outlying territories vulnerable and the crown deeply distracted.",["t"]="A Divided Court"}}}}}
t["subzone:stormwind-stockade"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,322,20.626.0,32.583.1,46.230.0,39.264.0,61.332.0,67.307.0",["h"]="0fd7d9",["n"]="Mazmorras de Ventormenta",["s"]="Mazmorras de Ventormenta. Escondidas bajo los canales a lo largo del borde norte del Barrio de los Magos, Las Mazmorras sirven como la penitenciaría de alta seguridad de Ventormenta. Destinada a encerrar a asesinos, disidentes políticos y enemigos extranjeros, la fortaleza subterránea se ha sumido recientemente en el caos absoluto tras una rebelión coordinada de los reclusos. Supervisadas habitualmente por el Alcaide Thelagua, Las Mazmorras son el lugar donde el reino confina a sus prisioneros más volátiles, que van desde degolladores y agentes Defias hasta orcos Roca Negra y enanos Hierro Negro capturados. Sin embargo, un violento levantamiento orquestado por el astuto conspirador Defias Bazil Thredd ha desbordado por completo a los guardias de la prisión. Los reclusos ahora deambulan libremente por las celdas inferiores, convirtiendo el recinto en una fortaleza amotinada. Thelagua, tras haber asegurado a duras penas los accesos principales, depende de aventureros independientes para adentrarse en los corredores subterráneos y reprimir la revuelta antes de que se extienda a los canales.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="The riot lays bare the operations of the Defias Brotherhood and Bazil Thredd, offering a glimpse into how deeply organized the criminal underworld has become right under the crown's nose.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Stockade sits directly in the capital, making its suppression vital to civil defense; clearing its halls exposes just how heavily the Defias Brotherhood has penetrated Stormwind."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The entrance sits along the canal district in Stormwind City, tucked on the northern bend right next to the bridge leading into the Mage Quarter. A guarded doorway leads down a stone stairwell directly into the subterranean cells.",["al"]={"stockade entrance","how to get to stockades","stockade location"},["q"]="Where is the entrance to the Stockade located?"},{["a"]="The revolt was planned and ignited by Bazil Thredd, a high-ranking Defias Brotherhood ringleader imprisoned within the compound. Under his command, the prisoners overpowered the guards, seized armaments, and established total control of the underground cellblocks.",["al"]={"who is bazil thredd","who leads the stockade riot","who runs the stockade"},["q"]="Who started the riot inside the prison?"},{["a"]="Stormwind captures high-priority hostiles from across its contested territories. Notably, Targorr the Dread was seized from the Redridge Mountains, and Kam Deepfury represents the Dark Iron threat. Rather than being swiftly executed, many were brought here as military prisoners or kept alive by noble decree for political leverage.",["al"]={"why are there orcs in stockades","dark iron prisoners stockade"},["q"]="Why are there orcs and Dark Iron dwarves in a Stormwind jail?"},{["a"]="Outlying settlements like Darkshire and Lakeshire sentenced criminals like Dextren Ward and Targorr the Dread to die, only to see the House of Nobles stay their executions. Frustrated by Stormwind's bureaucratic meddling, local leaders quietly enlist sellswords to bypass royal paperwork and finish the job.",["al"]={"duskwood stockade quest","crime and punishment","what comes around"},["q"]="Why are Duskwood and Redridge asking people to kill prisoners here?"}},["kw"]={"bazil thredd","canals","defias","dextren ward","kam deepfury","prison","riot","stockade","stormwind","targorr","warden thelwater"},["n"]="Stormwind Stockade",["s"]="Tucked away beneath the canals along the northern edge of the Mage Quarter, the Stockade serves as Stormwind's high-security penitentiary. Intended to lock away murderers, political dissidents, and foreign enemies, the subterranean fortress has recently collapsed into total chaos following a coordinated inmate rebellion.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Ordinarily overseen by Warden Thelwater, the Stockade is where the kingdom deposits its most volatile prisoners, ranging from cutthroats and Defias operatives to captured Blackrock orcs and Dark Iron dwarves. However, a violent uprising orchestrated by the cunning Defias conspirator Bazil Thredd has entirely displaced the prison guards. The inmates now roam freely in the lower cells, turning the fortress into a fortress of riots. Thelwater, having barely secured the entry thresholds, relies on independent adventurers to plunge into the subterranean corridors and suppress the revolt before it spills out into the canals.",["t"]="A Prison Under Siege"},{["b"]="The Stockade holds more than ordinary street convicts; it has long served as a bargaining chip for the kingdom's corrupt House of Nobles. Murderers and high-value prisoners who received death sentences elsewhere—such as the graverobber Dextren Ward from Duskwood or the Blackrock warlord Targorr the Dread from Redridge—have had their executions delayed by aristocratic interference to serve as political pawns. Even neighboring Ironforge has taken notice, covertly hiring mercenaries to execute dangerous inmates like Kam Deepfury when human bureaucracy stalls rightful justice.",["t"]="Bureaucracy and Backroom Schemes"}}}}}
t["subzone:stormwind-stockade-classic"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="28,265,18.586.0,27.590.1,30.162.0,36.231.0,64.239.0,60.218.0",["h"]="fdfe51",["n"]="Ventormenta Stockade (Classic)",["s"]="Ventormenta Stockade (Classic). Las Mazmorras de Ventormenta son una prisión subterránea fortificada situada bajo el distrito de los canales de Ciudad de Ventormenta. Construida en su origen para retener a delincuentes menores, mercenarios violentos y subversivos políticos, se ha sumido recientemente en el caos tras una violenta revuelta de reclusos. Ocultas junto a los canales entre Casco Antiguo y el Barrio de los Magos, las Mazmorras funcionan como la principal instalación penal del Reino de Ventormenta. Presidido por el Alcaide Thelagua, el complejo subterráneo alberga a una variedad de los malhechores más peligrosos del reino: degolladores de la Hermandad Defias, un orco Roca Negra merodeador, un ogro e incluso un enano Hierro Negro infiltrado. Recientemente, un motín carcelario coordinado y orquestado por el astuto criminal Bazil Thredd desbordó a la guarnición, expulsó a los guardias supervivientes y dejó a los convictos en pleno control de los pasillos interiores.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The riot directly beneath the capital's streets is an acute humiliation for Highlord Bolvar Fordragon's administration, showing how vulnerable Stormwind is from within while the king remains absent.",["race:Human"]="For humans of the outlying towns, the Stockade's dysfunction proves that the House of Nobles cares far more for legal red tape in the capital than protecting border settlements from murderers."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Stockade entrance is situated inside Stormwind City along the northern canal bank, bridging the passage between Old Town and the Cathedral and Mage districts.",["al"]={"stockade entrance","how to get to stockade","stockade location"},["q"]="Where is the Stockade located?"},{["a"]="While Warden Thelwater is the official warden, he was driven out during the rebellion. The facility is currently under the de facto control of the prisoner who instigated the uprising, Bazil Thredd, alongside allied Defias rioters.",["al"]={"who is in charge of stockade","stockade boss","bazil thredd"},["q"]="Who is currently running the prison?"},{["a"]="Stormwind holds high-value prisoners of war and saboteurs here. Targorr the Dread is a captured Blackrock orc raider from the nearby mountains, while Kam Deepfury is a hostile Dark Iron dwarf imprisoned for subversion against the Alliance.",["al"]={"why are there orcs in stockade","kam deepfury","targorr the dread"},["q"]="Why are there orcs and Dark Iron dwarves locked up in Stormwind?"},{["a"]="Bureaucracy and political interference from high-ranking Stormwind nobles repeatedly stalled executions for convicts like Dextren Ward and Targorr, sparking outrage from outer territories such as Redridge and Duskwood.",["al"]={"why werent they executed","stormwind nobles","dextren ward execution"},["q"]="Why were condemned murderers kept alive instead of executed?"}},["kw"]={"bazil thredd","defias","dextren ward","kam deepfury","prison","stockade","stormwind stockade","targorr the dread","uprising","warden thelwater"},["n"]="Stormwind Stockade (Classic)",["s"]="The Stormwind Stockade is a fortified underground prison beneath the canal district of Stormwind City. Originally built to contain petty criminals, violent mercenaries, and political subversives, it has recently plunged into chaos following a violent inmate revolt.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away off the canals between Old Town and the Mage Quarter, the Stockade serves as the primary penal facility of the Kingdom of Stormwind. Presided over by Warden Thelwater, the subterranean complex houses an assortment of the realm's most dangerous malefactors: cutthroats of the Defias Brotherhood, a marauding Blackrock orc, an ogre, and even an infiltrating Dark Iron dwarf. Recently, a coordinated prison riot orchestrated by the cunning felon Bazil Thredd overwhelmed the garrison, driving out surviving guards and leaving the convicts in full control of the interior halls.",["t"]="A Prison in Revolt"},{["b"]="The disaster within the Stockade exposes deep cracks in Stormwind's governance. Several notorious inmates, such as the Blackrock terror Targorr the Dread and the body-selling grave robber Dextren Ward, had long been sentenced to death, yet were kept alive due to endless stays of execution arranged by influential nobles. Frustrated by aristocratic stalling, neighboring settlements like Lakeshire and Darkshire, alongside the dwarven garrison at Dun Modr, have circumvented royal channels entirely, contracting outside adventurers to march in and execute key ringleaders amidst the bedlam.",["t"]="Bureaucracy and Retribution"}}}}}
t["subzone:strahnbrad"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="10,344,17.552.0,20.482.0,41.275.0,28.226.0,50.207.0,40.243.0",["h"]="79f77b",["n"]="Strahnbrad",["s"]="Strahnbrad. Strahnbrad es un asentamiento humano en ruinas situado en las alturas del noreste de las Montañas de Alterac, cerca de la frontera con las Tierras de la Peste del Oeste. Antaño famoso por ser el lugar de la temprana defensa del príncipe Arthas Menethil contra los asaltantes orcos Roca Negra, el pueblo ha caído desde entonces en la decadencia y sirve como bastión fortificado para la organización criminal de la Hermandad. Originalmente una posesión del reino de Alterac antes de ser absorbido por Lordaeron tras la Segunda Guerra, la desgracia de Strahnbrad comenzó en vísperas de la Tercera Guerra. Los orcos del Clan Roca Negra asaltaron el asentamiento para conseguir sacrificios humanos para la Legión Ardiente, lo que llevó al príncipe Arthas Menethil y a los Caballeros de la Mano de Plata a cabalgar en su defensa. Aunque Arthas expulsó a los asaltantes y abatió a su amo de esclavos, el pueblo sufrió un sangriento castigo. Cuando Lordaeron se desmoronó poco después a manos de la Plaga, Strahnbrad quedó abandonado a merced de los elementos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="Walking the cobblestones of Strahnbrad recalls the early, untainted days of Prince Arthas Menethil and Uther the Lightbringer, serving as a bitter reminder of how far Lordaeron's heroes have fallen.",["faction:Horde"]="The Syndicate's enslavement of the orc Gol'dir makes Strahnbrad an urgent target for Horde champions seeking to strike at human brigands and rescue their kin."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Strahnbrad was the site of the opening clash of the Third War for Prince Arthas Menethil. Sent by Uther the Lightbringer to protect the settlement from rampaging Blackrock orcs, Arthas made his first celebrated stand here, rescuing townsfolk and cutting down the orc raiders.",["al"]={"why does strahnbrad matter","arthas strahnbrad","strahnbrad history"},["q"]="Why is Strahnbrad significant in history?"},{["a"]="The Syndicate holds Strahnbrad. These human brigands, loyal to the fallen noble bloodlines of Alterac, have fortified the ruined town hall and blacksmith to use as a primary staging ground for their ambitions in the mountains.",["al"]={"who owns strahnbrad","strahnbrad mobs","who lives in strahnbrad"},["q"]="Who controls Strahnbrad now?"},{["a"]="Strahnbrad was originally part of the Kingdom of Alterac before the First War. After Alterac betrayed the Alliance during the Second War, the town was integrated under the domain of the Kingdom of Lordaeron.",["al"]={"is strahnbrad alterac or lordaeron","strahnbrad kingdom"},["q"]="Which kingdom did Strahnbrad belong to originally?"},{["a"]="The Syndicate captured an orc named Gol'dir and forced him into brutal slave labor within Strahnbrad's ruins. Horde operatives from Tarren Mill, directed by Krusk, send adventurers here to breach the Syndicate's defenses and break Gol'dir out.",["al"]={"horde quests in strahnbrad","krusk strahnbrad","gol'dir strahnbrad"},["q"]="Why does the Horde care about this town?"}},["kw"]={"alterac","arthas","blackrock","gol'dir","krusk","lordaeron","strahnbrad","syndicate"},["n"]="Strahnbrad",["s"]="Strahnbrad is a ruined human settlement nestled in the northeastern heights of the Alterac Mountains, near the border of the Western Plaguelands. Once famous as the site of Prince Arthas Menethil's early defense against Blackrock orc raiders, the town has since fallen into decay and serves as a fortified stronghold for the criminal Syndicate.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Originally a holding of the Kingdom of Alterac before being absorbed into Lordaeron following the Second War, Strahnbrad's misfortune began on the eve of the Third War. Blackrock clan orcs raided the settlement to take human sacrifices for the Burning Legion, leading Prince Arthas Menethil and the Knights of the Silver Hand to ride to its defense. Though Arthas drove the raiders away and slew their slave master, the town was heavily bloodied. When Lordaeron crumbled beneath the Scourge shortly thereafter, Strahnbrad was abandoned to the elements.",["t"]="A Town of Tragedy"},{["b"]="Today, Strahnbrad has become a crucial operations hub for the Syndicate, the organization of displaced Alteraci nobility and outlaws plotting to reclaim their fallen realm. Patrolled by human rogues and brigands, its abandoned town hall and blacksmith now serve as hideouts and staging grounds. The Syndicate uses the ruined town to house supplies and captive labor, including unfortunate prisoners like the orc Gol'dir, whom Horde scouts from Tarren Mill actively seek to liberate.",["t"]="The Syndicate's Grip"}}}}}
t["subzone:sun-rock-retreat"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,391,27.428.0,16.496.0,25.221.0,39.234.0,35.212.0,43.192.0",["h"]="802be5",["n"]="Refugio Roca del Sol",["s"]="Refugio Roca del Sol. El Refugio Roca del Sol es un santuario oculto de la Horda enclavado en lo alto de los picos centrales de Sierra Espolón, justo al sur del Lago Mirkfallon. Dominado por fuerzas de tauren y orcos, sirve como el principal punto de concentración y puesto de suministros de la Horda en la región. Más allá de su utilidad estratégica, el asentamiento se asienta sobre tierra sagrada venerada desde hace mucho tiempo por los tauren debido a su profunda resonancia espiritual. Escondido en una cuenca montañosa al sur del Lago Mirkfallon, el Refugio Roca del Sol ha tenido desde hace mucho tiempo una gran importancia espiritual para los tauren. Según la antigua tradición, An'she, el Sol, besó el mismísimo pico de la montaña donde se alza la aldea. Durante generaciones antes de la llegada de la Horda, chamanes y peregrinos tauren viajaban hasta aquí para realizar rituales que tendían puentes sobre el velo mortal, extrayendo fuerza del poderoso vínculo de esta tierra con el mundo de los espíritus.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="As the Horde's main staging hub in the Stonetalon Mountains, Sun Rock Retreat offers a vital resupply post and flight hub amidst contested peaks.",["race:Tauren"]="Sun Rock Retreat is more than an outpost to the shu'halo; it is sacred ground blessed by An'she, where shamans have walked the spirit realm for centuries."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Sun Rock Retreat is the primary Horde outpost in the Stonetalon Mountains. Inhabited mainly by tauren and orcs, it acts as a peaceful sanctuary, trading station, and command post for Horde champions working in the region.",["al"]={"what is sun rock","sun rock retreat info","who runs sun rock retreat"},["q"]="What is Sun Rock Retreat?"},{["a"]="Tauren legend holds that An'she, the Sun, touched the mountain where the retreat now stands. The land has an enduring connection to the spirit world, making it an ancient pilgrimage site for vision quests and communion with ancestors.",["al"]={"why is sun rock sacred","anshe stonetalon","tauren sun rock lore"},["q"]="Why is this place sacred to the tauren?"},{["a"]="The retreat contends with aggressive territorial harpies, hostile night elves guarding the sacred woods, and the destructive mining and logging efforts of the Venture Company, which ravages the natural landscape.",["al"]={"sun rock threats","who is attacking sun rock","stonetalon enemies"},["q"]="What threats does the retreat face?"},{["a"]="Sun Rock Retreat provides wind rider service connecting travelers directly to major central Kalimdor locations, including the Crossroads in the Barrens and the tauren capital of Thunder Bluff.",["al"]={"sun rock flight paths","flying to sun rock retreat","sun rock flight master"},["q"]="Where does the local flight master connect?"}},["kw"]={"an'she","mirkfallon lake","stonetalon mountains","sun rock retreat","sunrock","tauren","venture company"},["n"]="Sun Rock Retreat",["s"]="Sun Rock Retreat is a hidden Horde sanctuary nestled high within the central peaks of the Stonetalon Mountains, just south of Mirkfallon Lake. Dominated by tauren and orcish forces, it serves as the Horde's primary staging ground and supply post in the region. Beyond its strategic utility, the settlement rests upon sacred ground long revered by the tauren for its deep spiritual resonance.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away in a mountain basin south of Mirkfallon Lake, Sun Rock Retreat has long held spiritual importance for the tauren. According to ancient tradition, An'she, the Sun, kissed the very mountain peak where the village stands. For generations before the Horde's arrival, tauren shamans and pilgrims journeyed here to perform rituals bridging the mortal veil, drawing strength from the land's strong bond to the spirit world.",["t"]="A Sacred Haven in the Peaks"},{["b"]="Today, Sun Rock Retreat serves as the Horde's principal base of operations across the Stonetalon Mountains. Orcs and tauren work side by side to establish a secure foothold against hostile harpy broods, local night elf sentinels, and the industrial pillaging of the Venture Company. As a central hub connecting trade and flight routes between Thunder Bluff, the Crossroads, and the borders of Ashenvale, the retreat provides shelter, provisions, and spiritual guidance to those braving the crags.",["t"]="Frontier Outpost"}}}}}
